{"parentUuid":"c741a4d8-0078-4da0-9453-f963568060d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"04b90b0f-8126-4ccf-bbcf-bbcb2b29a279","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eSbT1XuMpVwMX4gBLfEXS","type":"tool_result","content":"=== RECALL: detached background spawn decisions ===\n - constraints.invariants.general | Killing an existing backfill from `brain stop` using its recorded PID and the distill-lock heuristic was rejected: setup records persist after completion, PIDs can be reused, and another distill pass can hold the lock, risking SIGKILL of an unrelated process; \n - architecture.data.flow | Synchronous entity-delta computation in the checkpoint hook was rejected after a measured 3.5-second stall; detached backfill keeps computation off the hook path, and synchronous computation should be reconsidered only with evidence that it meets the hook late\n - architecture.boundaries.rationale | The user chose machine-wide pause/resume for background brain work; a shared durable pause marker coordinates the watcher, memory workers, setup backfill, and session-end hook because killing processes cannot prevent launchd restarts or event-triggered launche\n - architecture.data.flow | The accepted onboarding plan makes the deterministic brain usable first, runs newest-first session backfill in the background, registers the repository with the shared daemon, and exposes extraction progress separately from doctor health checks so slow agent w\n - workflow.testing.rules | Synchronous entity-delta computation in checkpoint hooks was rejected after real graph runs took about 3.5 seconds per session, exceeding Codex's 2-second session-end budget, while a roughly 50-commit range exceeded the 10-second producer timeout; use detached\n - constraints.invariants.general | Killing backfills using the recorded PID plus the distill-lock heuristic was rejected: setup records persist after completion, PIDs can be reused, and another distill pass can hold the lock, risking termination of an unrelated process; revisit only with reliab\n - architecture.boundaries.rationale | Batching checkpoint hints into one spawn per commit was rejected because it requires a cross-repository repeatable --session contract change, multi-session commits are rare, and the plugin already throttles bursts; revisit if multi-session spawn overhead becom\n - workflow.testing.rules | Session-end hook tests must stub memoryWorkerLaunch: otherwise they spawn a worker whose working directory is inside t.TempDir(), preventing Windows from deleting the directory during cleanup.\n - constraints.filesystem.portability | Capturing directory identity through an open handle was considered for Windows rename verification, but a real Windows probe showed the handle blocks the rename; revisit only with a handle strategy proven to permit renaming.\n - architecture.data.flow | Making backgroundPaused return errors was rejected because unreadable pause markers deliberately mean “not paused,” while status warnings address pause visibility; revisit only if the fail-open policy changes.\n\n=== how is detachedSysProcAttr actually used? ===\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go:9:// detachedSysProcAttr has no session concept to use on Windows; the child is\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go:12:func detachedSysProcAttr() *syscall.SysProcAttr {\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_unix.go:9:// detachedSysProcAttr puts the backfill in its own session so it outlives the\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_unix.go:11:func detachedSysProcAttr() *syscall.SysProcAttr {\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn.go:21://   - a new session/process group (see detachedSysProcAttr), so the child is not\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn.go:44:\tcmd.SysProcAttr = detachedSysProcAttr()\n\n=== the spawn call site (stdio really redirected?) ===\n(internal/cli/setup_spawn.go)\n1-package cli\n2-\n3-import (\n4-\t\"errors\"\n5-\t\"fmt\"\n6-\t\"os\"\n7-\t\"os/exec\"\n8-\t\"path/filepath\"\n9-\t\"strings\"\n10-\n11-\t\"github.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli/internal/brainstore\"\n12-\t\"github.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli/internal/parentwatch\"\n13-)\n14-\n15-// spawnDetached starts the background backfill and returns immediately with the\n16-// child's pid. Detachment is the whole point: the prompt must come back the\n17-// instant the deterministic core is built, while an O(sessions) distill pass\n18-// keeps running — surviving the terminal that started it.\n19-//\n20-// Three properties make that true:\n21://   - a new session/process group (see detachedSysProcAttr), so the child is not\n22-//     killed by the shell's SIGHUP or a Ctrl-C aimed at setup;\n23-//   - stdio pointed at a log file and /dev/null, never at the parent's terminal,\n24-//     so a background run can never scribble over the user's prompt;\n25-//   - Release(), so no goroutine is left waiting on the child.\n26-func spawnDetached(plan setupBackfillPlan) (int, error) {\n27-\tif plan.Binary == \"\" {\n28-\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"no executable to run\")\n29-\t}\n30-\tif plan.LogPath != \"\" {\n31-\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(plan.LogPath), 0o700); err != nil {\n32-\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"create log directory: %w\", err)\n33-\t\t}\n34-\t}\n35-\tcmd := exec.Command(plan.Binary, plan.Args...)\n36-\tcmd.Dir = plan.Dir\n37-\tcmd.Env = plan.Env\n38-\t// Exempt every detached child from the parent-death watchdog, whoever the\n39-\t// caller: outliving the spawner is the point of this function, and the\n40-\t// daemon-reregister child's parent dies by design (launchctl bootout).\n41-\t// Environ copies plan.Env (or os.Environ when nil), so the caller's slice\n42-\t// is never written to.\n43-\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Environ(), parentwatch.DetachedEnv+\"=1\")\n44:\tcmd.SysProcAttr = detachedSysProcAttr()","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"816dc38c-762e-4b60-bef1-58a5b8419575","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:34:57.963Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== RECALL: detached background spawn decisions ===\n - constraints.invariants.general | Killing an existing backfill from `brain stop` using its recorded PID and the distill-lock heuristic was rejected: setup records persist after completion, PIDs can be reused, and another distill pass can hold the lock, risking SIGKILL of an unrelated process; \n - architecture.data.flow | Synchronous entity-delta computation in the checkpoint hook was rejected after a measured 3.5-second stall; detached backfill keeps computation off the hook path, and synchronous computation should be reconsidered only with evidence that it meets the hook late\n - architecture.boundaries.rationale | The user chose machine-wide pause/resume for background brain work; a shared durable pause marker coordinates the watcher, memory workers, setup backfill, and session-end hook because killing processes cannot prevent launchd restarts or event-triggered launche\n - architecture.data.flow | The accepted onboarding plan makes the deterministic brain usable first, runs newest-first session backfill in the background, registers the repository with the shared daemon, and exposes extraction progress separately from doctor health checks so slow agent w\n - workflow.testing.rules | Synchronous entity-delta computation in checkpoint hooks was rejected after real graph runs took about 3.5 seconds per session, exceeding Codex's 2-second session-end budget, while a roughly 50-commit range exceeded the 10-second producer timeout; use detached\n - constraints.invariants.general | Killing backfills using the recorded PID plus the distill-lock heuristic was rejected: setup records persist after completion, PIDs can be reused, and another distill pass can hold the lock, risking termination of an unrelated process; revisit only with reliab\n - architecture.boundaries.rationale | Batching checkpoint hints into one spawn per commit was rejected because it requires a cross-repository repeatable --session contract change, multi-session commits are rare, and the plugin already throttles bursts; revisit if multi-session spawn overhead becom\n - workflow.testing.rules | Session-end hook tests must stub memoryWorkerLaunch: otherwise they spawn a worker whose working directory is inside t.TempDir(), preventing Windows from deleting the directory during cleanup.\n - constraints.filesystem.portability | Capturing directory identity through an open handle was considered for Windows rename verification, but a real Windows probe showed the handle blocks the rename; revisit only with a handle strategy proven to permit renaming.\n - architecture.data.flow | Making backgroundPaused return errors was rejected because unreadable pause markers deliberately mean “not paused,” while status warnings address pause visibility; revisit only if the fail-open policy changes.\n\n=== how is detachedSysProcAttr actually used? ===\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go:9:// detachedSysProcAttr has no session concept to use on Windows; the child is\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go:12:func detachedSysProcAttr() *syscall.SysProcAttr {\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_unix.go:9:// detachedSysProcAttr puts the backfill in its own session so it outlives the\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn_unix.go:11:func detachedSysProcAttr() *syscall.SysProcAttr {\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn.go:21://   - a new session/process group (see detachedSysProcAttr), so the child is not\ninternal/cli/setup_spawn.go:44:\tcmd.SysProcAttr = detachedSysProcAttr()\n\n=== the spawn call site (stdio really redirected?) ===\n(internal/cli/setup_spawn.go)\n1-package cli\n2-\n3-import (\n4-\t\"errors\"\n5-\t\"fmt\"\n6-\t\"os\"\n7-\t\"os/exec\"\n8-\t\"path/filepath\"\n9-\t\"strings\"\n10-\n11-\t\"github.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli/internal/brainstore\"\n12-\t\"github.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli/internal/parentwatch\"\n13-)\n14-\n15-// spawnDetached starts the background backfill and returns immediately with the\n16-// child's pid. Detachment is the whole point: the prompt must come back the\n17-// instant the deterministic core is built, while an O(sessions) distill pass\n18-// keeps running — surviving the terminal that started it.\n19-//\n20-// Three properties make that true:\n21://   - a new session/process group (see detachedSysProcAttr), so the child is not\n22-//     killed by the shell's SIGHUP or a Ctrl-C aimed at setup;\n23-//   - stdio pointed at a log file and /dev/null, never at the parent's terminal,\n24-//     so a background run can never scribble over the user's prompt;\n25-//   - Release(), so no goroutine is left waiting on the child.\n26-func spawnDetached(plan setupBackfillPlan) (int, error) {\n27-\tif plan.Binary == \"\" {\n28-\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"no executable to run\")\n29-\t}\n30-\tif plan.LogPath != \"\" {\n31-\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(plan.LogPath), 0o700); err != nil {\n32-\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"create log directory: %w\", err)\n33-\t\t}\n34-\t}\n35-\tcmd := exec.Command(plan.Binary, plan.Args...)\n36-\tcmd.Dir = plan.Dir\n37-\tcmd.Env = plan.Env\n38-\t// Exempt every detached child from the parent-death watchdog, whoever the\n39-\t// caller: outliving the spawner is the point of this function, and the\n40-\t// daemon-reregister child's parent dies by design (launchctl bootout).\n41-\t// Environ copies plan.Env (or os.Environ when nil), so the caller's slice\n42-\t// is never written to.\n43-\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Environ(), parentwatch.DetachedEnv+\"=1\")\n44:\tcmd.SysProcAttr = detachedSysProcAttr()","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4aa9fc3d-5ee7-4a23-b2f1-e9bf8e7cdc35","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","branch":"win/full-support","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibil