{"parentUuid":"97082090-1277-4982-9e63-a63d69e91eba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwUSb5kTLqF2xsXwR6Yj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":359781,"output_tokens":1863,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":810},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":359781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11742,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"7b475ec3-2e86-4300-8ffe-a85fbdfea708","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwUSaWGp2eoUspkCJpUt","requestRef":"809c55e1-11e1-4710-8cf6-54b8fd04e4b8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ce0a112-b345-45b1-9c9b-33e6f336a370","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:42:01.536Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"8ce0a112-b345-45b1-9c9b-33e6f336a370","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwUSb5kTLqF2xsXwR6Yj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five of the nine brain items are done. Status, with the honest limits:\n\n**Done and verified locally:**\n\n1. **Store path** — brain now reads `%LOCALAPPDATA%` on Windows and ignores `XDG_DATA_HOME` there, matching cli. Scoped to the *data* dir only; config/state/cache already agreed, and `ResolvePluginDirs` has 71 callers so I didn't touch the general rule. Five tests, and I weakened the guard to prove the key one actually goes red.\n2. **Detached backfill** — now `DETACHED_PROCESS | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP`. **Correction to my own plan:** I'd written `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, but Microsoft documents that as undefined combined with `DETACHED_PROCESS`. cli's shipping version uses the pair above, so I matched it. The old comment claimed redirected stdio already detached the child from the console — it doesn't; that's why closing the terminal killed the backfill.\n3. **`ProcessAlive`** — was `os.FindProcess` only, which succeeds for an *exited* process whose handle is still open. That meant `backfillRunning` could see a finished backfill as live and the brain would quietly never backfill again. Now uses `WaitForSingleObject`, which is unambiguous — deliberately not `GetExitCodeProcess`, since `STILL_ACTIVE` is 259 and 259 is also a legal exit code.\n7. **Atomic replace** — `internal/config` made a single attempt while `brainstore` retried 100× on sharing/lock violations. Now consistent. They stay duplicated because Go's internal-package rule makes `brainstore` unimportable from `config`, which is the same reason `filelock_windows.go` exists three times.\n\n**4. Long paths — this one I'd flagged as absence-of-evidence, and the measurement is worth your attention.** Brain's own relative export path is **277 characters** worst case, before the store root starts. Win32's limit is 260 including the root. It works today only because Go rewrites long *absolute* paths to `\\\\?\\` form internally. So the margin isn't tight, it's negative — and anything outside Go's `os` package (git without `core.longpaths`, a backup tool, Explorer, zipping the store) can't address a deep export path at all. I added a budget test pinned in both directions so a layout change can't quietly grow it. I did **not** add a speculative `core.longpaths` fix, because I haven't proven brain actually hits it via git.\n\n**What I can't verify:** items 2 and 3 are behavioural on Windows. They compile and vet clean for amd64 and arm64, the repo's lint gate passes, and the Windows-only regression test I wrote will run on brain's CI leg — but that only happens on a push, and nothing is pushed. Treat those two as unverified until then.\n\nNothing merged, nothing pushed. Work is on local branch `win/full-support` in a worktree.\n\nRemaining: CRLF parity, the OneDrive/WAL doctor warning, the 12 skipped test files, and the ARM64 CI leg. Carrying on with those."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":359781,"output_tokens":1863,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":810},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":359781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7b475ec3-2e86-4300-8ffe-a85fbdfea708","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwUSaWGp2eoUspkCJpUt","requestRef"