{"parentUuid":"b37f00bd-7b1e-4fa1-bc65-ddb4f7bcd7b1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd0c8ca5-23f4-4bcd-88a6-2a91eca8e739","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E21ZWhD9bwn4QkUEyyWyDQ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== blame on the exclude line ===\nc0398da4 2026-05-25 Initial commit\n\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/test.yml b/.github/workflows/test.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..60c33b2e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/test.yml\n@@ -0,0 +30,3 @@\n+        exclude:\n+          - { goos: windows, goarch: arm64 }\n+    steps:\n\n=== recall: windows arm64 build decisions ===\n - Shipping entire-sem into benchmark containers was rejected after Linux cross-compilation hit internal/sem/zsh build constraints; build graphs natively on the host and expose NDJSON through graph-query\n - `entire graph impact` was tested as a value-add for Go refactor tasks (signature changes with 5–8 cross-file callers) and found no benefit: `go build ./... && go vet ./...` already provides an authori\n - On Linux CI, Docker's VM OOM-kills the sqlite dependency compile under default parallelism; constrained build parallelism is required to complete the build.\n - The Windows CI check \"test (windows-latest) / coverage and integrity\" appearing stuck/pending for ~10 minutes is a fan-in illusion: it waits for compile-and-plan (~3m15s) + 8 parallel shards (~3.5–5m \n - Terminal-Bench was dropped and its adapter removed after execution was blocked by missing API credentials and an arm64 Docker host running amd64 task images; reconsider only if the user restores this \n - `installedDaemonUnitPlan` resolves for the *host* service manager at compile/test time — tests that assert launchd verbs unconditionally will fail on Linux (systemd) and Windows (unsupported, empty Un\n\n=== does release actually ship windows/arm64? ===\n(eval):18: no matches found: .goreleaser.y*ml","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f309a100-250c-46f9-970c-6362525de00c","timest