{"parentUuid":"e029b671-710e-4b82-aab2-dd6e4dff9552","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwVpEVj19wAQth2JyX3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q1eYoT1tn8uncbkNjsUfLx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nr() { entire brain remember \"$1\" --path \"$2\" --json 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import sys,json\ntry: d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"  recorded\", d.get(\"id\",\"?\"))\nexcept Exception: print(\"  (no json)\")'; }\n\nr 'On Windows the brain and the host CLI resolved DIFFERENT plugin data roots: cli pluginParentDir uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins and ignores XDG_DATA_HOME there, while brain ResolveXDGDir used XDG then %USERPROFILE%\\.local\\share. Dispatched runs were fine (host sets ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR) but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different, EMPTY store with no error. Invariant: brain plugin DATA root must mirror cli pluginParentDir per-OS; config/state/cache already agree everywhere and must not be changed with it. Fixed via resolvePluginDataRoot(pluginDir, goos) in internal/cli/internal/base/env.go.' architecture.integration.gotcha\n\nr 'Brain export tree relative path is 277 characters worst case (sessions/branches/<slug80>-<hash8>/<ts16>_<agent32>_<session80>_<checkpoint32>.jsonl), which alone exceeds the Win32 MAX_PATH of 260 BEFORE the store root. It works only because Go os rewrites long ABSOLUTE paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form (os/path_windows.go fixLongPath) and the store root is always absolute. Margin is therefore zero and the guarantee is a Go implementation detail: anything outside Go os (git without core.longpaths, backup tools, Explorer, zipping the store) cannot address a deep export path. Pinned by TestExportRelativePathStaysWithinItsBudget.' constraints.filesystem.portability\n\nr 'evidenceHash is CRLF-SENSITIVE by design: evidenceBlocks deliberately preserves original CRLF so code fences and table rows survive verbatim, so the same commit checked out with core.autocrlf=true on Windows yields different digests than an LF checkout. Block STRUCTURE is CRLF-insensitive (TrimSpace eats the carriage return). Consequence: fact anchors are not portable across LF/CRLF checkouts, which matters for bundles and facts sync between a Windows and a Linux machine, not for single-machine use. Pinned by TestEvidenceHashIsCRLFSensitive.' constraints.filesystem.portability\n\nr 'entire-brain release.yml and nightly.yml both SHIP windows/arm64, but .github/workflows/test.yml build matrix excluded that exact target from the initial commit with no recorded reason, so the one published target was never compiled on a pull request. Removed the exclude; GOOS=windows GOARCH=arm64 go build ./... passes clean.' workflow.ci.gotcha","description":"Record four durable Windows findings in brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2185,"cache_read_input_tokens":389129,"output_tokens":1427,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":293},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2185,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":389129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2185},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q1eYoT1tn8uncbkNjsUfLx":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nr() { entire brain remember \"$1\" --path \"$2\" --json 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import sys,json\ntry: d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"  recorded\", d.get(\"id\",\"?\"))\nexcept Exception: print(\"  (no json)\")'; }\n\nr 'On Windows the brain and the host CLI resolved DIFFERENT plugin data roots: cli pluginParentDir uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins and ignores XDG_DATA_HOME there, while brain ResolveXDGDir used XDG then %USERPROFILE%\\.local\\share. Dispatched runs were fine (host sets ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR) but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different, EMPTY store with no error. Invariant: brain plugin DATA root must mirror cli pluginParentDir per-OS; config/state/cache already agree everywhere and must not be changed with it. Fixed via resolvePluginDataRoot(pluginDir, goos) in internal/cli/internal/base/env.go.' architecture.integration.gotcha\n\nr 'Brain export tree relative path is 277 characters worst case (sessions/branches/<slug80>-<hash8>/<ts16>_<agent32>_<session80>_<checkpoint32>.jsonl), which alone exceeds the Win32 MAX_PATH of 260 BEFORE the store root. It works only because Go os rewrites long ABSOLUTE paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form (os/path_windows.go fixLongPath) and the store root is always absolute. Margin is therefore zero and the guarantee is a Go implementation detail: anything outside Go os (git without core.longpaths, backup tools, Explorer, zipping the store) cannot address a deep export path. Pinned by TestExportRelativePathStaysWithinItsBudget.' constraints.filesystem.portability\n\nr 'evidenceHash is CRLF-SENSITIVE by design: evidenceBlocks deliberately preserves original CRLF so code fences and table rows survive verbatim, so the same commit checked out with core.autocrlf=true on Windows yields different digests than an LF checkout. Block STRUCTURE is CRLF-insensitive (TrimSpace eats the carriage return). Consequence: fact anchors are not portable across LF/CRLF checkouts, which matters for bundles and facts sync between a Windows and a Linux machine, not for single-machine use. Pinned by TestEvidenceHashIsCRLFSensitive.' constraints.filesystem.portability\n\nr 'entire-brain release.yml and nightly.yml both SHIP windows/arm64, but .github/workflows/test.yml build matrix excluded that exact target from the initial commit with no recorded reason, so the one published target was never compiled on a pull request. Removed the exclude; GOOS=windows GOARCH=arm64 go build ./... passes clean.' workflow.ci.gotcha","description":"Record four durable Windows findings in brain"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"badb8273-2e4c-43d3-92a2-bb876be52903","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwVpE6QvRFwrfYZxrf5Q","requestRef":"89f73b30-79fd-4694-8c02-0f32163dd993","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d6f27a34-6f93-41fb-a6b4-4b3ea9e1a417","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:00:08.756Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
