{"parentUuid":"2107c563-43b8-4234-8e73-5a4b6d9a42e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwW1FBTgmEfcLr84hWgR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the Track 2 deliverable — the cli PR review notes the plan committed to."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":406435,"output_tokens":3046,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3046,"cache_read_input_tokens":406435,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8612b6a6-9307-4c8e-b58c-b4a75a15efad","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwW1EpNqteiU4S6z64VQ","requestRef":"c14e5655-0773-4522-a2c6-1e51c892c776","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"82a614aa-bbe4-49f3-a884-cc95e9fb7c83","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:02:22.930Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"82a614aa-bbe4-49f3-a884-cc95e9fb7c83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwW1FBTgmEfcLr84hWgR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019zAGDeDHZzzE2xmXdxopiD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/WINDOWS-PR-REVIEW-NOTES.md","content":"# cli Windows PR queue — review notes and landing order\n\nRead-only review, 2026-11-11, against `entireio/cli` `origin/main` (`5870b2cd5`).\n**Nothing here was merged, approved, closed, rebased or commented on.** Every\n\"close this\" or \"pick this one\" is a recommendation for you.\n\n## The headline: this queue is authorship-blocked, not review-blocked\n\nI told you earlier it was ~3 weeks of finished work waiting on review. That was\nwrong, and the correction matters:\n\n- **6 of 10 are CONFLICTING**, some catastrophically. #1396 is **6509** commits\n  behind main; #1708 is 5049; #2352 is 3039; #2754 is 1465. Those are rewrites.\n- **5 of 7 inspected have never run a single CI check.** They are fork PRs, and\n  fork PRs need a maintainer to approve workflows before anything runs. So\n  \"the engineering exists\" has no verification behind it.\n- **2 of 7 are already superseded by main**, in whole or in part.\n\nThe systemic read still holds, though: cli has **268 open PRs, 244\n`REVIEW_REQUIRED`, 7 approved**. Review starvation is real and repo-wide — it is\njust not the binding constraint on *these*.\n\n## Landing order (the part that matters more than the reviews)\n\n### 0. Approve workflows on the fork PRs first\n\nThe single cheapest unblock, and only you can do it. Until it happens, #3070,\n#3071, #3102 and #1708 have zero CI signal and no reviewer can responsibly\njudge them.\n\n### 1. `#2754` **or** `#3099` — foundation, must be first\n\nBoth fix `osroot` directory handles preventing `t.TempDir` cleanup on Windows.\n#2754's own commit reports this was **502 of 542** strategy-package failures on\na Windows runner. **Every Windows test added by #3070/#3071/#3102 is unreliable\nuntil one lands.**\n\nThey are duplicates of each other — `ForgetUnder` (#2754) vs `ForgetTree`\n(#3099), same three files (`osroot/osroot.go`, `osroot/osroot_test.go`,\n`testutil/testutil.go`). Pick one; the other needs rewriting.\n\n- **#2754** (Soph, org branch): +309/-124 across 23 files, almost entirely test\n  work. **Has real CI: 17 checks green including `test-windows` and\n  `test-canary-windows`.** CONFLICTING, 1465 behind, and it touches\n  `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — the repo's hottest conflict file.\n- **#3099** (SparshM8, fork): +74/-0 across 3 files. Much smaller. No CI ever run.\n\n*My read:* #2754 is the better-evidenced change and the only one with a green\nWindows leg, but it is the harder rebase. #3099 is the faster path to unblocking\nthe others. If you want movement this week, land #3099 and ask #2754 to drop its\nosroot half.\n\n### 2. `#3070` vs `#3102` — pick one, do not review both\n\nBoth close issue **#3052**, both edit `execx/execx_windows.go` **and**\n`procutil/procutil_windows.go`. Reviewing both is wasted capacity.\n\n- **#3070** (Beehtrix): +780/-50 across 9 files. New `treekill_windows.go`\n  (+322), +382 test lines, deletes `procutil_unix.go`'s duplicated 28 lines,\n  unifies on `execx.KillTreeOnCancel`, adds `docs/development/git-safety.md`.\n  MERGEABLE.\n- **#3102** (SparshM8): +234/-7 across 4 files, single commit, +114 test lines,\n  in-place patch, no docs, no unification. MERGEABLE.\n\n*My read:* **#3070.** It is the design; #3102 is the patch. Both are mergeable,\nso this is a straight choice, not a sequencing problem.\n\n### 3. `#3071` — proclive on Windows (the data-loss one)\n\nThis is the highest-user-impact item in the whole queue. Without it,\n`OwnerExited()` can never fire on Windows, so:\n- an agent killed **mid-turn** shows ACTIVE for an hour, then \"stale\";\n- an agent killed **between turns** (IDLE) is **never flagged at all**, and\n  after 7 days `Clear()` deletes the state file along with uncondensed\n  checkpoint work.\n\nSubstance: +578/-48 across 11 files, with `proc_windows.go` (+185) and\n`proc_windows_test.go` (**+265**). Four commits, each addressing a real Win32\nsemantic — PID reuse via per-boot sequence number, the `STILL_ACTIVE`=259\nambiguity, SYNCHRONIZE-denied DACLs, WSL/native hostname collision. **This is\nnot a sketch.**\n\nBlockers: CONFLICTING, zero CI ever run, and its only real-world validation is\nan external volunteer (`mattjes`) hand-running it on Windows 11 — who reported\n`TestInitializeSession_CapturesOwner` failing, which is the `t.TempDir` bug\n**#2754/#3099 fixes**. It also depends on **#3055** by the author's own\nstatement, and #3055 is itself open, CONFLICTING and +2747/-98.\n\n*My read:* worth the effort, but it is third in line for real reasons.\n\n### 4. `#1396` — **close it**\n\nSuperseded. `origin/main` already has a 22-file `interactive` package with\n`tty_windows.go`, `console_windows.go`, `rawmode_windows.go` and tests, opening\n`CONIN$`. Main's version is **strictly better**: it opens `O_RDWR`, because\nBubble Tea's `SetConsoleMode` raw-mode switch needs `GENERIC_WRITE`. #1396 opens\n`O_RDONLY` and would regress raw-mode prompts. It also adds no tests, has run no\nCI, and has sat untouched for 155 days with 0 reviews and 0 comments.\n\nThat is abandonment, not a review queue. Reviewing it produces zero value.\n\n### 5. `#2352` — needs to shed code before review\n\nHalf of it landed via **#2349** in September. `HookHostIsWindows` is on main, and\nmain's `cursor/hooks.go` already does the sh↔cmd.exe migration through\n`UseWindowsProductionHooks`. The author predicted this in the commit body. Only\nthe BOM half is unlanded (`skipUTF8BOM`: zero hits on main).\n\nAlso worth knowing: its 10 \"reviews\" are **9 self-reviews** plus one Copilot. No\nexternal human has looked at it.\n\n### 6. `#1708` — WSL browser, lowest priority\n\n+444/-111, CONFLICTING, 5049 behind, no CI. Rewrites `login.go`, which main has\nsince rebuilt onto `OpenPromptTTY`, so a head-on collision is guaranteed. Also\ndrags unrelated `.opencode/package-lock.json` churn.\n\n## Two corrections to my own earlier numbers\n\n- \"10 open Windows-titled PRs, all awaiting review\" → **9**. #3075 is a DRAFT,\n  and a draft is not waiting on anyone.\n- The title filter **undercounts badly**. `--search \"windows\"` across bodies\n  returns ~60 open PRs, 15+ of which are substantive Windows work that is not\n  Windows-titled (#3099, #3095, #3093, #3091, #3101, #3056, #3055, #2966,\n  #2078, #2112, #2975). If the scope is \"Windows support\", the real queue is\n  2-3x what a title search shows.\n\n## Not in this queue, but cheap and mine\n\ncli has **no `.gitattributes`** at all, while brain has a good targeted one\n(embedded `go:embed` assets and golden fixtures pinned to LF, each rule carrying\nthe bug it prevents). Measured: **0 committed CRLF files in cli**, so porting\nbrain's file breaks nothing today and prevents a class of Windows-only golden\ntest failures later. Report-only — cli is not my lane.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":406435,"output_tokens":3046,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3046,"cache_read_input_tokens":406435,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019zAGDeDHZzzE2xmXdxopiD":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaa