{"parentUuid":"5d1aa99a-3641-4123-b854-2b507ae06829","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwWLhXWq6D9zYK7AkNXh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still running — `internal/cli` is the long pole. Committing the doc work meanwhile (markdown only, doesn't affect the running suite)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":428328,"output_tokens":1097,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":428328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b5f784ae-1ba9-443b-919a-5a06a53232bd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwWLhCfHYRDxTt82TSno","requestRef":"6c0bb133-8ed2-4fb6-b747-92de2720a3e2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"29d39098-28f3-4d6d-8ec8-4cbf726cf299","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:06:51.564Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"29d39098-28f3-4d6d-8ec8-4cbf726cf299","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwWLhXWq6D9zYK7AkNXh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017jQefV1KTHmd6HLeSx26QV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\ngit add docs/limits.md\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@aisprouts.ngo\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ndocs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narrow a lock claim\n\nTwo Windows facts the file either omitted or overstated.\n\nThe export tree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, which exceeds\nWin32's 260 before the store root is counted. It works only because Go\nrewrites long absolute paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form, which covers Brain's\nown I/O and nothing else -- git without core.longpaths, backup agents,\nExplorer and user scripts all still see an over-length path. Says so, and\npoints at LongPathsEnabled as the setting that removes the dependency for\nevery tool rather than just this one.\n\nThe path-safety section claimed lock files \"open with O_NOFOLLOW and reject\nsymlinks, hardlinks, and open-file aliasing\". That is true on Unix and only\nhalf true on Windows, where fileLockOpenFlags returns 0: the post-open\nGetFileInformationByHandle check still rejects hardlinks, but the open\nfollows a symlink. Stating one guarantee for both platforms made the weaker\none look like the stronger one.\nMSG\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -2\necho \"unpushed: $(git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD) commit(s), nothing pushed\"","description":"Commit the documentation corrections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":428328,"output_tokens":1097,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":428328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017jQefV1KTHmd6HLeSx26QV":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\ngit add docs/limits.md\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@aisprouts.ngo\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ndocs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narrow a lock claim\n\nTwo Windows facts the file either omitted or overstated.\n\nThe export tree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, which exceeds\nWin32's 260 before the store root is counted. It works only because Go\nrewrites long absolute paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form, which covers Brain's\nown I/O and nothing else -- git without core.longpaths, backup agents,\nExplorer and user scripts all still see an over-length path. Says so, and\npoints at LongPathsEnabled as the setting that removes the dependency for\nevery tool rather than just this one.\n\nThe path-safety section claimed lock files \"open with O_NOFOLLOW and reject\nsymlinks, hardlinks, and open-file aliasing\". That is true on Unix and only\nhalf true on Windows, where fileLockOpenFlags returns 0: the post-open\nGetFileInformationByHandle check still rejects hardlinks, but the open\nfollows a symlink. Stating one guarantee for both platforms made the weaker\none look like the stronger one.\nMSG\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -2\necho \"unpushed: $(git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD) commit(s), nothing pushed\"","description":"Commit the documentation corrections"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b5f784ae-1ba9-443b-919a-5a06a53232bd","apiBlockI