{"parentUuid":"756db820-1f32-44b4-aae5-54694d5910de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwWV3Krd1ciiorztWBKs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Full module suite passed: **42 packages ok, 0 failures, exit 0**. That closes the last verification I control — it's the regression check that mattered, since `env.go` has 71 callers and I'd only tested four packages before.\n\n## Done\n\nBrain's Windows work is complete and committed locally — two commits on `win/full-support` in a worktree, **nothing pushed, nothing merged, no PR**.\n\nEight of nine plan items landed: store path now agrees with the host CLI, detached backfill actually survives the terminal, `ProcessAlive` no longer reports finished backfills as running, atomic-replace retry parity, a doctor warning for OneDrive/UNC stores, CRLF parity pinned, the 277-char path limit measured and documented, and `windows/arm64` restored to the build matrix.\n\nThe ninth — draining 22 Windows test skips — I declined, and verified rather than assumed: they're Unix mode bits and group/other permission assertions that Windows genuinely lacks. Porting them means ACL rewrites for no coverage gain.\n\nVerification: lint gate green, host and `GOOS=windows` amd64 + arm64 build clean, full suite green, and one guard weakening-tested to prove it actually catches its bug.\n\n## Over to you\n\n**Run** `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/windows-verify.ps1` from the worktree root on your Windows box. Two caveats I'd rather state than paper over: I can't syntax-check it (no `pwsh` here), and I found a real defect in it on re-reading — it would have written into and deleted from your actual `%LOCALAPPDATA%` brain store. It now uses a throwaway temp root.\n\n**One check it can't do:** run `entire brain setup` in a repo, then close the terminal while the backfill is still going. It should survive now, with no console flash.\n\n**Decisions in `WINDOWS-PR-REVIEW-NOTES.md`:** approve fork workflows (cheapest unblock, only you can), land #2754-or-#3099 first, pick #3070 over #3102, and close #1396 as superseded.\n\nThe thing I'd flag hardest: the 277-char export path works today only because Go quietly rewrites long absolute paths to `\\\\?\\`. Nothing outside Go's `os` package gets that — not git, not backup tools, not Explorer. The margin isn't thin, it's zero, and it's resting on a standard-library implementation detail."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":434210,"output_tokens":1058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":213},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1058,"cache_read_input_tokens":434210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f83262ba-01d4-4a4d-9d89-345cb6f9741a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwWV2v3wqngwH4xWc6Lx","requestRef":"de1004a4-00b6-4d9b-ac79-72e2a0b4063b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"c92f91f6-b666-45ec-ad91-c1fa825fb40e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:08:51.922Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
