{"parentUuid":"170d0af3-8b41-4e11-a0f7-8cb6b614f723","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwX7rRoPYSNHKZvitZBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PowerShell container is still starting — likely emulated, and this machine is at load 11. I'll report when it lands.\n\nWhile it runs, let me be direct about the goal rather than restating the same handoff a third time.\n\nThe `finish` condition as the hook reads it requires Windows execution. I have no Windows machine, and the two routes to one are both closed by your own instructions: pushing to trigger brain's Windows CI leg (which *would* run the real suite, the `ProcessAlive` regression test, and the long-path behaviour) is exactly what \"no merging or pushing till we already fully ready\" forbids. So the condition isn't one I can satisfy by working harder at it.\n\nThree ways out, your call:\n\n1. **Keep the handoff as-is** — you run `windows-verify.ps1` plus the terminal-close check. This is what you asked for when you said you'd test on your Windows box, and it's the only option that doesn't change a standing rule.\n2. **Let me push `win/full-support`** to its own branch so brain's Windows CI runs it. That leg is a real required full sharded suite, so it would genuinely close the verification gap — but it means pushing, which you've told me twice not to do. I won't without you saying so explicitly.\n3. **Clear the goal** if you're treating my half as the deliverable, since the rest is yours by design.\n\nI'd take (1), with (2) available the moment you want CI evidence rather than my word.\n\nThe one thing I'm still closing myself is the script syntax check, so what I hand you isn't unvalidated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":439094,"output_tokens":802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":305},"server