{"parentUuid":"5a2c8496-632f-4d41-95b5-5f8eaa8a6c5b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwZcUWid4eeVTTZH51p6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011YL7k5r3aWm9PujnReNnt1","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"The 'finish' goal keeps failing because the approved plan requires Windows verification (store path, ProcessAlive, detached backfill, long-path write, Windows suite). I have no Windows machine, and brain's CI only runs on push-to-main, a PR, or a manual workflow_dispatch — so nothing I can do from here satisfies it. How do you want to resolve it?","header":"Resolve goal","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"You test, I stand down (Recommended)","description":"You run windows-verify.ps1 on your Windows box plus the manual terminal-close check, which is what you said you'd do. I've validated the script as far as a Linux PowerShell container allows. Nothing gets pushed, your standing rule holds, and the goal gets cleared because my half is done. Report back and I'll fix whatever it finds."},{"label":"Push branch + manual dispatch","description":"I push win/full-support (no PR) and you trigger the workflow manually on that branch, which runs brain's full required Windows leg: the sharded suite, my ProcessAlive regression test, and the arm64 build I re-enabled. Real CI evidence instead of my word. Overrides your no-push rule for this one branch, so I need you to say it explicitly."},{"label":"Open a draft PR","description":"Pushing plus a draft PR triggers CI automatically with no manual dispatch needed. Strongest verification and the normal workflow, but it creates a PR, which crosses your 'no PRs till my review' rule the most directly of the three."},{"label":"Keep working on something else","description":"Leave Windows verification parked entirely and point me at different work. The brain changes stay committed locally and unverified on Windows until you get to them."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1256,"cache_read_input_tokens":450864,"output_tokens":1188,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":405},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1256,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":450864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1256},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011YL7k5r3aWm9PujnReNnt1":{"questions":[{"question":"The 'finish' goal keeps failing because the approved plan requires Windows verification (store path, ProcessAlive, detached backfill, long-path write, Windows suite). I have no Windows machine, and brain's CI only runs on push-to-main, a PR, or a manual workflow_dispatch — so nothing I can do from here satisfies it. How do you want to resolve it?","header":"Resolve goal","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"You test, I stand down (Recommended)","description":"You run windows-verify.ps1 on your Windows box plus the manual terminal-close check, which is what you said you'd do. I've validated the script as far as a Linux PowerShell container allows. Nothing gets pushed, your standing rule holds, and the goal gets cleared because my half is done. Report back and I'll fix whatever it finds."},{"label":"Push branch + manual dispatch","description":"I push win/full-support (no PR) and you trigger the workflow manually on that branch, which runs brain's full required Windows leg: the sharded suite, my ProcessAlive regression test, and the arm64 build I re-enabled. Real CI evidence ins