- Capture hooks are off (`.entire/settings.json` has `enabled: false`,\n  `.claude/settings.json` removed) so a throwaway clone does not attribute\n  checkpoints to the wrong repository. Kit-local; not part of the fix.\n- The project's own README is in the `baseline` commit:\n  `git show baseline:README.md`.\n\n## The honest state of the evidence\n\nAlready done, on macOS, and therefore weaker than it sounds:\n\n- full module suite 42 packages ok, 0 failures\n- `gofmt -l -s` and `go vet` clean for host and `GOOS=windows`\n- builds clean for windows/amd64, windows/arm64, linux/arm64\n\nNot done, and not doable from macOS — this is the whole point of the kit:\n\n- the store path a standalone `entire-brain.exe` actually resolves\n- whether a detached backfill survives its terminal closing\n- whether a 277-character export path can be written\n- whether the doctor warning fires on a OneDrive-redirected store\n- whether the suite is green on Windows rather than Darwin\nEOF\ncd \"$KIT\"\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" commit -q -m \"test kit: instructions, verify script, and results template\n\nEverything an independent tester needs to execute the five Windows checks\nthat cannot be run from macOS, plus an honest map of what each check does\nand does not prove.\n\nKit-local changes that are NOT part of the fix: capture hooks disabled\n(.entire/settings.json enabled:false, .claude/settings.json removed) so a\nthrowaway clone cannot attribute checkpoints to the wrong repository, and\nREADME/CLAUDE.md replaced to point at the protocol. The originals are in\nthe baseline commit.\"\ngit log --oneline\necho \"=== size ===\"\ndu -sh \"$KIT/.git\"","description":"Write README and commit the test kit"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6e4ab052-482f-4dfd-aef8-560adafeebd7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch7kemGQckdLSTossqNDU","requestRef":"a1045789-cbde-4294-9663-e2f873595ad6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":