{"parentUuid":"51eb71ac-4bd4-4ba5-be44-51088f8a5d4a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9Dbhp6uEzvwKeNRDTE3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Committing the fixes as reviewable units."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1627,"cache_read_input_tokens":278624,"output_tokens":2781,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":894},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1627,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2781,"cache_read_input_tokens":278624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1627},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"defc4b5f-91fa-497c-b008-4f324d60acd1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9DbhYEPqJPgbi3WoeQ9","requestRef":"95db7959-9d8d-4c21-b420-e7456b64bd48","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d28b2d3a-68c1-41e1-b334-50355cd70c91","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:34:30.918Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"d28b2d3a-68c1-41e1-b334-50355cd70c91","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9Dbhp6uEzvwKeNRDTE3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BBbdFqyT6r7ZULDZZSrz8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nset -e\n\ngit add internal/cli/doctor_synced_store.go internal/cli/doctor_synced_store_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent\n\nThe OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows -- the only platform it\nexists for. pathIsUnder normalised separators to \"/\" and then called\nfilepath.Clean, which on Windows turns them straight back into \"\\\". The\ncomponent check that followed looked for a prefix ending in \"/\", so it\nnever matched.\n\nEvery one of the six tests covering it is written with Windows-shaped\nbackslash paths, and every one passed on darwin, where filepath.Clean\nleaves \"/\" alone. That is how a dead code path reached a Windows machine\nwith a green suite behind it: the subject was OS-dependent while the\ntests were not, so they measured darwin and reported Windows.\n\nNormalising with package path instead makes the comparison identical\neverywhere, which is also what turns those six into real cross-OS tests.\nAdds TestSyncedStoreComparisonIsOSIndependent for the mixed-separator and\nsibling-prefix cases, and a source-level guard that fails if path/filepath\nis reintroduced into this file -- the comment saying not to would not have\nsurvived the next edit.\n\nFound by running the verification kit on Windows 11:\nTestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows failed 3/3.\nEOF\necho \"1/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/internal/clitest/clitest.go internal/cli/main_test.go internal/cli/testhome_test.go internal/cli/root_test.go internal/cli/internal/base/env_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root\n\nMaking the brain read %LOCALAPPDATA% on Windows broke test isolation\nthere, because clitest.PinXDGRoots -- the TestMain of 25 packages -- pins\nonly the four XDG variables. So on Windows every test that resolved the\ndefault store walked out of the sandbox and into the developer's real\n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire. A plain `go test ./...` created and populated a\nreal brain store on the machine that found this.\n\nThis is the same mistake testhome_test.go was written to prevent, one\nlevel down: redirect HOME, forget USERPROFILE, stay green on every POSIX\nshard. The lesson did not generalise because the fix was a helper rather\nthan a rule, so the rule is written down now.\n\n- PinXDGRoots pins LOCALAPPDATA too, on every OS rather than under a\n  GOOS check: a pin that only exists on the platform that needs it cannot\n  be checked by the platforms that run most of the CI.\n- redirectHomeDir redirects it as well, mirroring the real layout under\n  the redirected home so the variable and the %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\n  fallback agree.\n- TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots walks clitest.PinnedRoots instead of its own\n  list, so a variable added to the sandbox is checked automatically and\n  one removed from it cannot quietly stop being checked.\n- TestResolvePluginDataRootHonoursASandboxedEnvironmentOnEveryOS loops\n  over the target OS. That is the guard that was missing: every other\n  test here resolves only the rule for the OS it was compiled for.\n- TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks expects the LOCALAPPDATA answer on Windows\n  rather than asserting an XDG path the product deliberately no longer\n  produces there.\n\nRegression found by the verification kit on Windows 11; all three tests\npassed on baseline and failed on the fix.\nEOF\necho \"2/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/memory_cmd.go internal/cli/memory_worker_selfexec_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary\n\nlaunchDetachedSelf re-execs os.Executable(). Under `go test` that is the\npackage's own test binary, which does not understand \"memory worker\n--once\": it treats them as positional arguments and re-runs the whole\npackage, which reaches launchDetachedSelf again.\n\nOn a Windows machine where the enclosing directory happened to be a git\nrepository, that built a chain of 34 test binaries, each the child of the\nlast, one more every 15-75 seconds. The chain outlived the run, timed\ninternal/cli out at ten minutes (it passes in 376s without it), held the\ntest binary open against deletion, and -- because every link re-ran the\nfull suite in the wrong repository -- wrote agent setup files into the\nuser's home directory.\n\nRefuses under `go test`, detected by test-binary name and by the test.v\nflag, because either signal alone can be absent. Checked through package\nflag rather than testing.Testing() so the testing package stays out of\nthe shipped binary, where it would register its flags for real.\n\nTests that need the launch observed already inject memoryWorkerLaunch.\nThis path is the one nothing injects, so it fails closed, and\nTestLaunchDetachedSelfRefusesUnderGoTest calls it uninjected -- the only\ntest in the package that can catch the refusal being removed.\nEOF\necho \"3/6 committed\"\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the first three fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1627,"cache_read_input_tokens":278624,"output_tokens":2781,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":894},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1627,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2781,"cache_read_input_tokens":278624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1627},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":24062,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013BBbdFqyT6r7ZULDZZSrz8":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nset -e\n\ngit add internal/cli/doctor_synced_store.go internal/cli/doctor_synced_store_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent\n\nThe OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows -- the only platform it\nexists for. pathIsUnder normalised separators to \"/\" and then called\nfilepath.Clean, which on Windows turns them straight back into \"\\\". The\ncomponent check that followed looked for a prefix ending in \"/\", so it\nnever matched.\n\nEvery one of the six tests covering it is written with Windows-shaped\nbackslash paths, and every one passed on darwin, where filepath.Clean\nleaves \"/\" alone. That is how a dead code path reached a Windows machine\nwith a green suite behind it: the subject was OS-dependent while the\ntests were not, so they measured darwin and reported Windows.\n\nNormalising with package path instead makes the comparison identical\neverywhere, which is also what turns those six into real cross-OS tests.\nAdds TestSyncedStoreComparisonIsOSIndependent for the mixed-separator and\nsibling-prefix cases, and a source-level guard that fails if path/filepath\nis reintroduced into this file -- the comment saying not to would not have\nsurvived the next edit.\n\nFound by running the verification kit on Windows 11:\nTestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows failed 3/3.\nEOF\necho \"1/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/internal/clitest/clitest.go internal/cli/main_test.go internal/cli/testhome_test.go internal/cli/root_test.go internal/cli/internal/base/env_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root\n\nMaking the brain read %LOCALAPPDATA% on Windows broke test isolation\nthere, because clitest.PinXDGRoots -- the TestMain of 25 packages -- pins\nonly the four XDG variables. So on Windows every test that resolved the\ndefault store walked out of the sandbox and into the developer's real\n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire. A plain `go test ./...` created and populated a\nreal brain store on the machine that found this.\n\nThis is the same mistake testhome_test.go was written to prevent, one\nlevel down: redirect HOME, forget USERPROFILE, stay green on every POSIX\nshard. The lesson did not generalise because the fix was a helper rather\nthan a rule, so the rule is written down now.\n\n- PinXDGRoots pins LOCALAPPDATA too, on every OS rather than under a\n  GOOS check: a pin that only exists on the platform that needs it cannot\n  be checked by the platforms that run most of the CI.\n- redirectHomeDir redirects it as well, mirroring the real layout under\n  the redirected home so the variable and the %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\n  fallback agree.\n- TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots walks clitest.PinnedRoots instead of its own\n  list, so a variable added to the sandbox is checked automatically and\n  one removed from it cannot quietly stop being checked.\n- TestResolvePluginDataRootHonoursASandboxedEnvironmentOnEveryOS loops\n  over the target OS. That is the guard that was missing: every other\n  test here resolves only the rule for the OS it was compiled for.\n- TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks expects the LOCALAPPDATA answer on Windows\n  rather than asserting an XDG path the product deliberately no longer\n  produces there.\n\nRegression found by the verification kit on Windows 11; all three tests\npassed on baseline and failed on the fix.\nEOF\necho \"2/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/memory_cmd.go internal/cli/memory_worker_selfexec_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary\n\nlaunchDetachedSelf re-execs os.Executable(). Under `go test` that is the\npackage's own test binary, which does not understand \"memory worker\n--once\": it treats them as positional arguments and re-runs the whole\npackage, which reaches launchDetachedSelf again.\n\nOn a Windows machine where the enclosing directory happened to be a git\nrepository, that built a chain of 34 test binaries, each the child of the\nlast, one more every 15-75 seconds. The chain outlived the run, timed\ninternal/cli out at ten minutes (it passes in 376s without it), held the\ntest binary open against deletion, and -- because every link re-ran the\nfull suite in the wrong repository -- wrote agent setup files into the\nuser's home directory.\n\nRefuses under `go test`, detected by test-binary name and by the test.v\nflag, because either signal alone can be absent. Checked through package\nflag rather than testing.Testing() so the testing package stays out of\nthe shipped binary, where it would register its flags for real.\n\nTests that need the launch observed already inject memoryWorkerLaunch.\nThis path is the one nothing injects, so it fails closed, and\nTestLaunchDetachedSelfRefusesUnderGoTest calls it uninjected -- the only\ntest in the package that can catch the refusal being removed.\nEOF\necho \"3/6 committed\"\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the first three fixes"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"defc4b5f-91fa-497c-b008-4f324d60acd1","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch9DbhYEPqJPgbi3WoeQ9","requestRef":"95db7959-9d8d-4c21-b420-e7456b64bd48","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"55ae9b5d-e7ea-4e4a-b00f-a3ce77bbfcee","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:34:54.982Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
