{"parentUuid":"593da3ab-7e86-419e-a301-866990faf014","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14824619 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ac9e020b-9d5b-427e-9582-8809421dd8a6","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:35:43.602Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14824619 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"ac9e020b-9d5b-427e-9582-8809421dd8a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9Di1Nx38dNXWsdgq6KX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y3oM83q81jH8N9BS7LXjCq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nset -e\n\ngit add internal/cli/symlink_test.go internal/agentsetup/agents_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/brain_brief_git_intent_test.go internal/cli/brain_brief_precedent_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/brain_manifest_read_test.go internal/cli/history_fts_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/memory_abstract_hardening_test.go internal/cli/memory_hardening_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/pattern_corpus_publish_test.go internal/cli/repo_key_guard_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/review_source_availability_test.go internal/cli/semantic_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/skill_write_escape_test.go internal/cli/workspace_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\n\nWindows refuses os.Symlink for an unprivileged account without Developer\nMode -- \"A required privilege is not held by the client\". Thirty-two\ntests treated that as a failure, so a plain `go test ./...` on an\nordinary Windows machine produced a wall of red that said nothing about\nthe product and buried the two real regressions in it.\n\ninternal/agentsetup already had the right idiom and simply did not apply\nit in its symlinkForTest helper; internal/cli had no helper at all. Both\nnow probe the capability and skip on a privilege refusal, failing loudly\nfor every other error so a genuinely broken fixture still fails.\n\nDeliberately not a blanket runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" skip. Developer\nMode, an elevated shell and the CI runners all do provide symlinks, and\nWindows is exactly where the os.Root and path semantics these tests cover\nmost need exercising. Probe the capability; never assume it from the\nplatform.\n\nThe classifier is unit-tested against a fabricated ERROR_PRIVILEGE_NOT_HELD,\nbecause no real call on a POSIX machine ever produces one -- it would\notherwise ship untested on the only platform it exists for.\nEOF\necho \"4/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/agent_wiring.go internal/cli/agent_wiring_home_guard_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings\n\ninstallPreEditHook merges a PreToolUse entry into\n<repo>/.claude/settings.json, and the comment above it argues this is\nsafe because project settings merge with the user's rather than replacing\nthem. That argument stops holding in exactly one case: when the\nrepository root IS the home directory, the two files are the same file.\n\nOn a Windows machine whose C:\\Users\\<user> was itself a git repository, a\nrun resolved that as the repo root and merged the hook into the user's\nglobal Claude Code settings, where it stayed -- firing on every edit in\nevery session on the machine, for every project.\n\nRefuses rather than warns, because keeping a dotfiles repository in the\nhome directory is common enough that silently making a machine-global\nchange is the worse default. The caller already reports a hook error as\n\"pre-edit hook not wired\" without failing the step, so the guide still\nlands and the user is told which half did not.\n\nThe comparison reuses the synced-store normaliser: case insensitive and\nseparator independent, which is what %USERPROFILE% needs.\nEOF\necho \"5/6 committed\"\n\ngit add CONTRIBUTING.md docs/limits.md\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndocs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, and confirm the Go half\n\nThirteen tracked files under benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/ reach 215\ncharacters, so a stock Git for Windows cannot check this repository out:\n`git clone` fails with \"Filename too long\" until core.longpaths=true.\nMeasured, not predicted -- at a 48-character clone root all 13 are over\nthe 260 limit, and only a very short root such as C:\\b clears them.\n\nThat is the \"git subprocesses, unless the repository sets\ncore.longpaths=true\" bullet docs/limits.md already carried, now observed\non real hardware against our own repository, so both sides point at each\nother.\n\nAlso upgrades the long-path claim from reasoned to measured. On Windows\n11 with LongPathsEnabled=0, a probe through Go's os package wrote and\nread back a 383-character absolute path, while PowerShell 5.1's\nNew-Item -Force silently failed to create a 368-character directory on\nthe same machine -- no error, no directory. Both halves hold: Brain's own\nI/O survives the ceiling and the tools around it do not.\n\nDocumented rather than shortening the evidence paths: that is a rename of\ncommitted benchmark evidence and belongs in its own change.\nEOF\necho \"6/6 committed\"\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD\ngit status --short","description":"Commit the remaining three fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3004,"cache_read_input_tokens":280251,"output_tokens":1712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3004,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":280251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3004},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":18954,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y3oM83q81jH8N9BS7LXjCq":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\nset -e\n\ngit add internal/cli/symlink_test.go internal/agentsetup/agents_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/brain_brief_git_intent_test.go internal/cli/brain_brief_precedent_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/brain_manifest_read_test.go internal/cli/history_fts_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/memory_abstract_hardening_test.go internal/cli/memory_hardening_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/pattern_corpus_publish_test.go internal/cli/repo_key_guard_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/review_source_availability_test.go internal/cli/semantic_test.go \\\n  internal/cli/skill_write_escape_test.go internal/cli/workspace_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\n\nWindows refuses os.Symlink for an unprivileged account without Developer\nMode -- \"A required privilege is not held by the client\". Thirty-two\ntests treated that as a failure, so a plain `go test ./...` on an\nordinary Windows machine produced a wall of red that said nothing about\nthe product and buried the two real regressions in it.\n\ninternal/agentsetup already had the right idiom and simply did not apply\nit in its symlinkForTest helper; internal/cli had no helper at all. Both\nnow probe the capability and skip on a privilege refusal, failing loudly\nfor every other error so a genuinely broken fixture still fails.\n\nDeliberately not a blanket runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" skip. Developer\nMode, an elevated shell and the CI runners all do provide symlinks, and\nWindows is exactly where the os.Root and path semantics these tests cover\nmost need exercising. Probe the capability; never assume it from the\nplatform.\n\nThe classifier is unit-tested against a fabricated ERROR_PRIVILEGE_NOT_HELD,\nbecause no real call on a POSIX machine ever produces one -- it would\notherwise ship untested on the only platform it exists for.\nEOF\necho \"4/6 committed\"\n\ngit add internal/cli/agent_wiring.go internal/cli/agent_wiring_home_guard_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings\n\ninstallPreEditHook merges a PreToolUse entry into\n<repo>/.claude/settings.json, and the comment above it argues this is\nsafe because project settings merge with the user's rather than replacing\nthem. That argument stops holding in exactly one case: when the\nrepository root IS the home directory, the two files are the same file.\n\nOn a Windows machine whose C:\\Users\\<user> was itself a git repository, a\nrun resolved that as the repo root and merged the hook into the user's\nglobal Claude Code settings, where it stayed -- firing on every edit in\nevery session on the machine, for every project.\n\nRefuses rather than warns, because keeping a dotfiles repository in the\nhome directory is common enough that silently making a machine-global\nchange is the worse default. The caller already reports a hook error as\n\"pre-edit hook not wired\" without failing the step, so the guide still\nlands and the user is told which half did not.\n\nThe comparison reuses the synced-store normaliser: case insensitive and\nseparator independent, which is what %USERPROFILE% needs.\nEOF\necho \"5/6 committed\"\n\ngit add CONTRIBUTING.md docs/limits.md\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndocs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, and confirm the Go half\n\nThirteen tracked files under benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/ reach 215\ncharacters, so a stock Git for Windows cannot check this repository out:\n`git clone` fails with \"Filename too long\" until core.longpaths=true.\nMeasured, not predicted -- at a 48-character clone root all 13 are over\nthe 260 limit, and only a very short root such as C:\\b clears them.\n\nThat is the \"git subprocesses, unless the repository sets\ncore.longpaths=true\" bullet docs/limits.md already carried, now observed\non real hardware against our own repository, so both sides point at each\nother.\n\nAlso upgrades the long-path claim from reasoned to measured. On Windows\n11 with LongPathsEnabled=0, a probe through Go's os package wrote and\nread back a 383-character absolute path, while PowerShell 5.1's\nNew-Item -Force silently failed to create a 368-character directory on\nthe same machine -- no error, no directory. Both halves hold: Brain's own\nI/O survives the ceiling and the tools around it do not.\n\nDocumented rather than shortening the evidence paths: that is a rename of\ncommitted benchmark evidence and belongs in its own change.\nEOF\necho \"6/6 committed\"\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD\ngit status --short","description":"Commit the remaining three fixes"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b545a03f-6a99-4cd0-a32a-71185d97f0d0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch9DhzHUKjRYNRLWe4tpM","requestRef":"dde3b7da-54d7-4bb7-b59a-b7909cae708e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bef6d13a-108c-4014-87d0-6147aa653b1a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:36:03.760Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
