{"parentUuid":"e7896feb-4199-48d7-8795-f3353fcce5a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9E4XCdzxsSDxYAVjVin","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PARSE OK` (the assertion after it is QEMU noise — the parse already returned 0). Writing the protocol docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":301457,"output_tokens":4191,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4191,"cache_read_input_tokens":301457,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"793f1e56-b9ef-455a-92b5-0d0a48a79eee","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9E4WwFvxvdsht9SJLD1","requestRef":"197fa08b-fc8c-4178-bd35-05f80d8711c3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1eb40c1-a88a-4739-9565-0ec0021e1e0f","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:40:25.596Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"f1eb40c1-a88a-4739-9565-0ec0021e1e0f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9E4XCdzxsSDxYAVjVin","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EWFLyHryKBoxWS9wCx4rar","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncat > \"$KIT/TESTING.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification protocol — round 2\n\nRun this on a **real Windows machine**. Not WSL, not a Linux container, not\nWine. WSL is a Linux kernel and will pass checks that Windows fails; it is the\nexact false green this kit exists to avoid. The script refuses to run if `go env\nGOOS` is not `windows`.\n\nBudget about **20 minutes**, most of it the full suite in section 6.\n\n---\n\n## 0. What changed since round 1\n\nRound 1 found two regressions in the change, five pre-existing bugs, and five\nfaults in the kit. Everything below is now fixed; this round mostly confirms it.\n\n| Round 1 finding | Now |\n|---|---|\n| F1 store-path fix escaped the test sandbox into the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` | fixed — `LOCALAPPDATA` is pinned by the shared test sandbox on every OS |\n| F2 OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows | fixed — the comparison no longer uses `path/filepath` |\n| P1 tests wrote into the home folder, incl. **global** `.claude/settings.json` | guarded — setup refuses to write a hook when the repo root is the home dir |\n| P2 `launchDetachedSelf` re-exec chain, 34 processes, suite timeout | fixed — refuses to re-exec under `go test`, fails closed |\n| P3 32 tests failed instead of skipping without symlink privilege | fixed — both packages probe and skip |\n| P4 repo cannot be cloned without `core.longpaths` | documented in CONTRIBUTING.md |\n| P5 two `TestDegenerate*` failures, cause undetermined | **still open** — see section 7 |\n| K1 kit README broke 5 doc tests | fixed — project `README.md` untouched, kit text in `VERIFY-KIT.md` |\n| K2 commit count / diff range wrong | fixed — `baseline` and `fix-tip` tags bound the change |\n| K3 section 4 measured PowerShell, not the brain | fixed — Go probe in `verify/longpath/` |\n| K4 stray processes unchecked, no ceiling dirs | fixed — section 6 sets ceilings, section 7 counts strays |\n| K5 preflight blind to a home-directory repo | fixed — section 0 detects and warns |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Prerequisites\n\n| Need | Check | If missing |\n|---|---|---|\n| Windows 10/11, native | `go env GOOS` says `windows` | stop |\n| PowerShell 5.1 or `pwsh` 7+ | `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion` | ships with Windows |\n| Go 1.26+ | `go version` | https://go.dev/dl/ |\n| Git for Windows | `git --version` | one command under test is repo-scoped |\n\nOptional, and it changes what section 1 can prove: the host **`entire` CLI** on\nPATH. With it, section 1 runs the strong check (standalone and dispatched runs\nmust resolve the same store). Without it, only the weaker half runs. Do not\ninstall it just for this; report which you got.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Get the code\n\n```powershell\ngit clone -c core.longpaths=true <this repo's URL> brain-win\ncd brain-win\n```\n\n`core.longpaths=true` is not optional: 13 tracked files are long enough that a\nstock Git for Windows fails the checkout with `Filename too long`. That is\nfinding P4 and it is now documented in CONTRIBUTING.md, not fixed — the files\nare committed benchmark evidence and renaming them belongs in its own change.\n\nConfirm the tags:\n\n```powershell\ngit log --oneline baseline..fix-tip    # the change under test\ngit log --oneline fix-tip..HEAD        # this kit's own files, nothing else\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Run the script\n\n```powershell\npwsh -File windows-verify.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath verify-output.txt\n```\n\nor on PowerShell 5.1:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File windows-verify.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath verify-output.txt\n```\n\nIt prints `PASS` / `FAIL` / `WARN` / `..` per check and a summary. `..` is\ninformation, `WARN` is context about your machine, only `FAIL` counts.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What each section proves, and what it does not\n\n### Section 0 — preflight\n\nRecords whether a git repository encloses your temp or home directory. Round 1\nran on a machine where `C:\\Users\\<user>` was itself a repo, which changed many\nresults and caused real damage. It also records the state of the real store\n**before** anything runs, so section 7 can tell what this run created.\n\n### Section 1 — store path\n\nThe defect: a standalone `entire-brain.exe` read a different, empty store from\nthe one the host CLI uses, and said nothing. **Strong check** only with the host\nCLI present. Otherwise the fallback merely confirms the path sits under\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%`, which is necessary but not sufficient.\n\n### Section 2 — `ProcessAlive`\n\nWindows-only tests that have never run anywhere else. A finished backfill used\nto report as running forever.\n\n### Section 3 — the round-1 regressions and the new guards\n\nThis is the section this round exists for. It runs, by name, the three tests\nthat failed on the fix and passed on `baseline`, plus the OneDrive test that\nfailed 3/3, plus the five new guards. **A FAIL here means the fix for a known\ndefect did not work on Windows.**\n\n### Section 4 — long paths, through Go\n\nRound 1's probe used PowerShell 5.1, whose `New-Item -Force` *silently* fails at\n~368 characters — no exception, no directory. That measured PowerShell. Brain's\nexporter goes through Go's `os` package, which rewrites long absolute paths to\n`\\\\?\\` first. The probe in `verify/longpath/` reproduces the real 277-character\nexport layout and reads the file back.\n\nA **PASS with `LongPathsEnabled` = 0** is the informative result: it confirms\nthe margin is zero and that a Go implementation detail is the only thing holding\nit up. Do not enable the policy to make it pass; you would measure a different\nmachine.\n\n### Section 5 — the repo's own path lengths\n\nInformational. Confirms P4 is still true of the repository.\n\n### Section 6 — full suite\n\n`go test ./...`, with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set so repo discovery cannot\nwalk out of a temp directory into an enclosing repository. Round 1 showed that\nwalk starting a self-replicating chain of test binaries.\n\n### Section 7 — what the run left behind\n\nCounts stray test binaries, and compares the real store against the snapshot\ntaken in section 0. **A FAIL here means the sandbox escape is back.** It also\nflags `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `.entire\\agent-guide.md` in your home folder\nif they exist — round 1 created those, so they may be left over rather than new.\nCheck the timestamps.\n\n### Still not covered by the script\n\n- **Detached backfill** — needs a human closing a window. Section 5 below.\n- **Atomic-replace retry on sharing violations.** Nothing here reproduces a\n  `SHARING_VIOLATION`; it needs a second process holding the file open at the\n  instant of replace. The suite proves it compiles and does not regress.\n  **Honest gap. Do not report it as verified.**\n- **The windows/arm64 CI leg.** Only a CI run proves that, and nothing pushes.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The manual check (please do this one)\n\nStill unrun after round 1, because the host CLI was not installed. It is the\nmost user-visible fix in the set.\n\n```powershell\n# in some git repository on this machine, NOT this kit\nentire brain setup\n```\n\nThen, **while the background backfill is still running**, close the terminal\nwindow — click the X, do not Ctrl-C and do not `exit`.\n\n1. `entire-brain.exe` should **still be running** (Task Manager, or\n   `Get-Process entire-brain`). Before the fix it died with the console.\n2. **No console window should flash** when the backfill starts.\n\nIf the host CLI is not installed, say so — that is a legitimate \"not run\".\n\n> Deliberately **not** `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`: Microsoft documents that flag as\n> undefined combined with `DETACHED_PROCESS`. A brief flash may be the\n> documented tradeoff rather than a bug; report it rather than judging it.\n\n---\n\n## 6. If the full suite fails\n\nDo not report a failure as a regression until you have checked. The `baseline`\ntag exists for this, and round 1's use of it was the single most useful thing in\nthat report.\n\n```powershell\ngo test ./internal/cli -count=1          # on the fix: should reproduce\ngit checkout baseline\ngo test ./internal/cli -count=1          # on untouched upstream\ngit checkout -\n```\n\n- Fails on **both** → pre-existing, not caused by this change. Still report it,\n  labelled.\n- Fails only on the **fix** → a real regression, and the highest-value finding\n  available. Report the full output.\n\nUse `-count=1` to defeat the test cache. If a failure looks timing-related,\nre-run that one package alone before calling it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Known-open, do not re-diagnose unless you want to\n\n`TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and\n`TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failed on both the fix and\n`baseline` in round 1, in the `bare_repository` / `not_a_repository` subtests.\nThe cause was not determined and nothing in this round addresses it. If they\nstill fail, that is expected; if you happen to see **why**, that is a bonus\nfinding.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Things that are **not** bugs\n\n- `..` lines and `WARN` lines. Only `FAIL` counts.\n- \"host 'entire' CLI not on PATH\" — expected if you did not install it.\n- \"profile is not OneDrive-redirected\" — expected on most machines. The\n  OneDrive warning path then only gets unit coverage, not a live store.\n- Section 4 passing with `LongPathsEnabled` empty or 0 — the expected result.\n- Tests **skipping** with \"symlinks unavailable on this host\". That is finding\n  P3 fixed. Round 1 had 32 of these as failures.\n- Capture hooks doing nothing — kit-local, see `VERIFY-KIT.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Report back\n\nFill in `RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md`. What must be in it:\n\n1. Windows version, `go version`, `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion`, whether the host\n   `entire` CLI was present, whether a repo encloses your home or temp dir.\n2. The script's **full output**, verbatim.\n3. Per section: PASS / FAIL / NOT RUN, with exact text for anything but PASS.\n4. The manual detached-backfill result.\n5. For any suite failure, the attribution: pre-existing or regression.\n6. Anything you could not do and why.\n\n**Do not round a partial result up.** \"Section 1 ran only its weaker half\" is a\nuseful report; \"Section 1 passed\" implies a comparison that did not happen.\nEOF\necho \"TESTING.md: $(wc -l < \"$KIT/TESTING.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the round-2 testing protocol"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":301457,"output_tokens":4191,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4191,"cache_read_input_tokens":301457,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":49564,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EWFLyHryKBoxWS9wCx4rar":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncat > \"$KIT/TESTING.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification protocol — round 2\n\nRun this on a **real Windows machine**. Not WSL, not a Linux container, not\nWine. WSL is a Linux kernel and will pass checks that Windows fails; it is the\nexact false green this kit exists to avoid. The script refuses to run if `go env\nGOOS` is not `windows`.\n\nBudget about **20 minutes**, most of it the full suite in section 6.\n\n---\n\n## 0. What changed since round 1\n\nRound 1 found two regressions in the change, five pre-existing bugs, and five\nfaults in the kit. Everything below is now fixed; this round mostly confirms it.\n\n| Round 1 finding | Now |\n|---|---|\n| F1 store-path fix escaped the test sandbox into the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` | fixed — `LOCALAPPDATA` is pinned by the shared test sandbox on every OS |\n| F2 OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows | fixed — the comparison no longer uses `path/filepath` |\n| P1 tests wrote into the home folder, incl. **global** `.claude/settings.json` | guarded — setup refuses to write a hook when the repo root is the home dir |\n| P2 `launchDetachedSelf` re-exec chain, 34 processes, suite timeout | fixed — refuses to re-exec under `go test`, fails closed |\n| P3 32 tests failed instead of skipping without symlink privilege | fixed — both packages probe and skip |\n| P4 repo cannot be cloned without `core.longpaths` | documented in CONTRIBUTING.md |\n| P5 two `TestDegenerate*` failures, cause undetermined | **still open** — see section 7 |\n| K1 kit README broke 5 doc tests | fixed — project `README.md` untouched, kit text in `VERIFY-KIT.md` |\n| K2 commit count / diff range wrong | fixed — `baseline` and `fix-tip` tags bound the change |\n| K3 section 4 measured PowerShell, not the brain | fixed — Go probe in `verify/longpath/` |\n| K4 stray processes unchecked, no ceiling dirs | fixed — section 6 sets ceilings, section 7 counts strays |\n| K5 preflight blind to a home-directory repo | fixed — section 0 detects and warns |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Prerequisites\n\n| Need | Check | If missing |\n|---|---|---|\n| Windows 10/11, native | `go env GOOS` says `windows` | stop |\n| PowerShell 5.1 or `pwsh` 7+ | `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion` | ships with Windows |\n| Go 1.26+ | `go version` | https://go.dev/dl/ |\n| Git for Windows | `git --version` | one command under test is repo-scoped |\n\nOptional, and it changes what section 1 can prove: the host **`entire` CLI** on\nPATH. With it, section 1 runs the strong check (standalone and dispatched runs\nmust resolve the same store). Without it, only the weaker half runs. Do not\ninstall it just for this; report which you got.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Get the code\n\n```powershell\ngit clone -c core.longpaths=true <this repo's URL> brain-win\ncd brain-win\n```\n\n`core.longpaths=true` is not optional: 13 tracked files are long enough that a\nstock Git for Windows fails the checkout with `Filename too long`. That is\nfinding P4 and it is now documented in CONTRIBUTING.md, not fixed — the files\nare committed benchmark evidence and renaming them belongs in its own change.\n\nConfirm the tags:\n\n```powershell\ngit log --oneline baseline..fix-tip    # the change under test\ngit log --oneline fix-tip..HEAD        # this kit's own files, nothing else\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Run the script\n\n```powershell\npwsh -File windows-verify.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath verify-output.txt\n```\n\nor on PowerShell 5.1:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File windows-verify.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath verify-output.txt\n```\n\nIt prints `PASS` / `FAIL` / `WARN` / `..` per check and a summary. `..` is\ninformation, `WARN` is context about your machine, only `FAIL` counts.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What each section proves, and what it does not\n\n### Section 0 — preflight\n\nRecords whether a git repository encloses your temp or home directory. Round 1\nran on a machine where `C:\\Users\\<user>` was itself a repo, which changed many\nresults and caused real damage. It also records the state of the real store\n**before** anything runs, so section 7 can tell what this run created.\n\n### Section 1 — store path\n\nThe defect: a standalone `entire-brain.exe` read a different, empty store from\nthe one the host CLI uses, and said nothing. **Strong check** only with the host\nCLI present. Otherwise the fallback merely confirms the path sits under\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%`, which is necessary but not sufficient.\n\n### Section 2 — `ProcessAlive`\n\nWindows-only tests that have never run anywhere else. A finished backfill used\nto report as running forever.\n\n### Section 3 — the round-1 regressions and the new guards\n\nThis is the section this round exists for. It runs, by name, the three tests\nthat failed on the fix and passed on `baseline`, plus the OneDrive test that\nfailed 3/3, plus the five new guards. **A FAIL here means the fix for a known\ndefect did not work on Windows.**\n\n### Section 4 — long paths, through Go\n\nRound 1's probe used PowerShell 5.1, whose `New-Item -Force` *silently* fails at\n~368 characters — no exception, no directory. That measured PowerShell. Brain's\nexporter goes through Go's `os` package, which rewrites long absolute paths to\n`\\\\?\\` first. The probe in `verify/longpath/` reproduces the real 277-character\nexport layout and reads the file back.\n\nA **PASS with `LongPathsEnabled` = 0** is the informative result: it confirms\nthe margin is zero and that a Go implementation detail is the only thing holding\nit up. Do not enable the policy to make it pass; you would measure a different\nmachine.\n\n### Section 5 — the repo's own path lengths\n\nInformational. Confirms P4 is still true of the repository.\n\n### Section 6 — full suite\n\n`go test ./...`, with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set so repo discovery cannot\nwalk out of a temp directory into an enclosing repository. Round 1 showed that\nwalk starting a self-replicating chain of test binaries.\n\n### Section 7 — what the run left behind\n\nCounts stray test binaries, and compares the real store against the snapshot\ntaken in section 0. **A FAIL here means the sandbox escape is back.** It also\nflags `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `.entire\\agent-guide.md` in your home folder\nif they exist — round 1 created those, so they may be left over rather than new.\nCheck the timestamps.\n\n### Still not covered by the script\n\n- **Detached backfill** — needs a human closing a window. Section 5 below.\n- **Atomic-replace retry on sharing violations.** Nothing here reproduces a\n  `SHARING_VIOLATION`; it needs a second process holding the file open at the\n  instant of replace. The suite proves it compiles and does not regress.\n  **Honest gap. Do not report it as verified.**\n- **The windows/arm64 CI leg.** Only a CI run proves that, and nothing pushes.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The manual check (please do this one)\n\nStill unrun after round 1, because the host CLI was not installed. It is the\nmost user-visible fix in the set.\n\n```powershell\n# in some git repository on this machine, NOT this kit\nentire brain setup\n```\n\nThen, **while the background backfill is still running**, close the terminal\nwindow — click the X, do not Ctrl-C and do not `exit`.\n\n1. `entire-brain.exe` should **still be running** (Task Manager, or\n   `Get-Process entire-brain`). Before the fix it died with the console.\n2. **No console window should flash** when the backfill starts.\n\nIf the host CLI is not installed, say so — that is a legitimate \"not run\".\n\n> Deliberately **not** `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`: Microsoft documents that flag as\n> undefined combined with `DETACHED_PROCESS`. A brief flash may be the\n> documented tradeoff rather than a bug; report it rather than judging it.\n\n---\n\n## 6. If the full suite fails\n\nDo not report a failure as a regression until you have checked. The `baseline`\ntag exists for this, and round 1's use of it was the single most useful thing in\nthat report.\n\n```powershell\ngo test ./internal/cli -count=1          # on the fix: should reproduce\ngit checkout baseline\ngo test ./internal/cli -count=1          # on untouched upstream\ngit checkout -\n```\n\n- Fails on **both** → pre-existing, not caused by this change. Still report it,\n  labelled.\n- Fails only on the **fix** → a real regression, and the highest-value finding\n  available. Report the full output.\n\nUse `-count=1` to defeat the test cache. If a failure looks timing-related,\nre-run that one package alone before calling it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Known-open, do not re-diagnose unless you want to\n\n`TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and\n`TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failed on both the fix and\n`baseline` in round 1, in the `bare_repository` / `not_a_repository` subtests.\nThe cause was not determined and nothing in this round addresses it. If they\nstill fail, that is expected; if you happen to see **why**, that is a bonus\nfinding.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Things that are **not** bugs\n\n- `..` lines and `WARN` lines. Only `FAIL` counts.\n- \"host 'entire' CLI not on PATH\" — expected if you did not install it.\n- \"profile is not OneDrive-redirected\" — expected on most machines. The\n  OneDrive warning path then only gets unit coverage, not a live store.\n- Section 4 passing with `LongPathsEnabled` empty or 0 — the expected result.\n- Tests **skipping** with \"symlinks unavailable on this host\". That is finding\n  P3 fixed. Round 1 had 32 of these as failures.\n- Capture hooks doing nothing — kit-local, see `VERIFY-KIT.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Report back\n\nFill in `RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md`. What must be in it:\n\n1. Windows version, `go version`, `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion`, whether the host\n   `entire` CLI was present, whether a repo encloses your home or temp dir.\n2. The script's **full output**, verbatim.\n3. Per section: PASS / FAIL / NOT RUN, with exact text for anything but PASS.\n4. The manual detached-backfill result.\n5. For any suite failure, the attribution: pre-existing or regression.\n6. Anything you could not do and why.\n\n**Do not round a partial result up.** \"Section 1 ran only its weaker half\" is a\nuseful report; \"Section 1 passed\" implies a comparison that did not happen.\nEOF\necho \"TESTING.md: $(wc -l < \"$KIT/TESTING.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the round-2 testing protocol"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"793f1e56-b9ef-455a-92b5-0d0a48a79eee","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch9E4WwFvxvdsht9SJLD1","requestRef":"197fa08b-fc8c-4178-bd35-05f80d8711c3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1548c1e1-55da-4d9d-acf9-ab8ac5259345","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:41:15.161Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
