{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"97976766-4127-47c0-aa64-7566b84db59b","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:41:15.443Z","version":"2.1.323","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"f4fff458b21a0bb5071afb74bdd0bbc2795b9bef89e3489038486d11d2a9c472","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"197fa08b-fc8c-4178-bd35-05f80d8711c3","keep":245,"tail":["e919c4b04d6a8ac2643e7866efd66ed6a3c0eeaa48686f31e4b82306071c1774","399ffcb91244f521185094c8ef2be94a0bdae41dbaccd1e4896b0b5c9a8b54b8","7139ae82a6c99d8162b066b78a00b8ae0058a6dd52beecb5dc0d92028d119c8e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",247,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8af30eebc5541d99ad10620750cd10d52a6ea7ca0a32551317d3deb6c0a36b87"}
{"parentUuid":"93ac0bc1-b75d-48f1-ab08-61aa6bcee703","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14801706 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9cd25b2b-8ff0-40f0-b4e0-74e0ad73aec5","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:41:15.403Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14801706 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"9cd25b2b-8ff0-40f0-b4e0-74e0ad73aec5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9E8TGrsNnb1SwM7NW3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Mrs2YyVLXBupBfcCtwFhM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncat > \"$KIT/CHANGES.md\" <<'EOF'\n# What is under test\n\n`git diff baseline..fix-tip` is exactly this and nothing else. `HEAD` carries\none further commit holding only this kit's own files.\n\nEight commits: two from round 1 (the original Windows fix), six added after a\nreal Windows machine found what the first pass could not.\n\n## Round 1 — the original change\n\n### 1. Store path disagreed with the host — `internal/cli/internal/base/env.go`\n\nThe brain resolved its plugin **data** root through XDG on every OS. The host\nCLI ignores `XDG_DATA_HOME` on Windows and uses `%LOCALAPPDATA%`. Dispatched\nruns never hit it because the host sets `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` explicitly; a\nstandalone `entire-brain.exe` read a **different, empty store and said nothing**.\n\n- **Verified by:** script section 1 (needs Windows). Round 1 confirmed the path\n  resolves under `%LOCALAPPDATA%`; the strong standalone-vs-dispatched\n  comparison still needs the host CLI installed.\n\n### 2. Detached backfill died with the console — `internal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go`\n\n`CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` alone does not detach a child from its console, so\nclosing the terminal killed the background backfill. Adds `DETACHED_PROCESS`;\ndeliberately **not** `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, which Microsoft documents as undefined\nin that combination.\n\n- **Verified by:** the manual check in TESTING.md §5. **Still unrun** — round 1\n  had no host CLI installed.\n\n### 3. `ProcessAlive` never reported death — `.../brainstore/process_alive_windows.go`\n\n`os.FindProcess` succeeds for an exited process whose handle is still open, and\nholds exactly such a handle. A finished backfill reported as running forever.\nUses `WaitForSingleObject`, unambiguous where `GetExitCodeProcess`'s\n`STILL_ACTIVE` (259) is not.\n\n- **Verified by:** script section 2. **Green on Windows in round 1.**\n\n### 4. No warning for a synced or network store — `internal/cli/doctor_synced_store.go`\n\nSQLite WAL corrupts on a OneDrive-synced or UNC directory, and `%USERPROFILE%`\nis commonly OneDrive-redirected. Doctor now warns.\n\n- **Round 1 found this one broken** — see fix 5 below.\n\n### 5. Atomic replace gave up on the first sharing violation — `internal/config/atomic_replace_windows.go`\n\nAdds the same retry loop its `brainstore` twin has. The duplication is forced by\nGo's internal-package rule and is now commented as such.\n\n- **NOT VERIFIED.** Nothing reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`. The suite proves\n  it compiles and does not regress. Do not report it as verified.\n\n### 6. windows/arm64 shipped untested — `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\nThe test matrix excluded a target `release.yml` and `nightly.yml` both ship.\n\n- **NOT VERIFIABLE here.** Only a CI run proves it.\n\n### Documentation — `docs/limits.md`\n\nRecords the 277-character export-path ceiling and narrows a lock-file security\nclaim that was true on Unix and only half true on Windows.\n\n- Round 1 **confirmed** the Go half on real hardware: 383 characters written and\n  read back with `LongPathsEnabled=0`.\n\n---\n\n## Round 2 — what the Windows run found, and what was done\n\n### 7. The store-path fix escaped the test sandbox (regression)\n\n`clitest.PinXDGRoots` is the `TestMain` of 25 packages and pinned only the four\nXDG variables. Once the data root read `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, every test resolving a\ndefault store on Windows walked out of the sandbox into the developer's real\nstore — and a plain `go test ./...` **created and populated one**.\n\nThis is the same mistake `testhome_test.go` was written to prevent, one level\ndown: redirect `HOME`, forget `USERPROFILE`, stay green on every POSIX shard.\n\n- `PinXDGRoots` pins `LOCALAPPDATA`, on **every** OS — a pin that exists only on\n  the platform needing it cannot be checked by the platforms running the CI.\n- `redirectHomeDir` redirects it too, mirroring the real layout under the\n  redirected home.\n- `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots` walks `clitest.PinnedRoots()` rather than its own\n  list, so a variable added to the sandbox is checked automatically.\n- `TestResolvePluginDataRootHonoursASandboxedEnvironmentOnEveryOS` loops over\n  the **target OS**. That is the guard that was missing: every other test here\n  resolves only the rule for the OS it was compiled for.\n- **Verified by:** script section 3, and section 7's before/after store check.\n\n### 8. The OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows\n\n`pathIsUnder` normalised separators to `/` and then called `filepath.Clean`,\nwhich on Windows turns them straight back into `\\`. The component check looked\nfor a prefix ending in `/`, so on the only platform the branch exists for, it\nnever matched. All six tests use backslash paths and all six passed on darwin,\nwhere `filepath.Clean` leaves `/` alone.\n\nNow normalised with package `path`, which is identical on every OS — and that is\nwhat turns those six into real cross-OS tests. A source-level guard fails if\n`path/filepath` is reintroduced into that file.\n\n- **Verified by:** script section 3.\n\n### 9. Setup could write a hook into the user's **global** Claude settings\n\n`installPreEditHook` merges into `<repo>/.claude/settings.json`, and the comment\nabove it argued this is safe because project settings merge with the user's.\nThat stops holding when the repository root **is** the home directory: the two\nare the same file. On the round-1 machine, `C:\\Users\\<user>` was a git repo, so\na run merged a `PreToolUse` hook into the user's global settings, where it fired\non every edit in every Claude Code session on the machine.\n\nNow refused, with the reason reported. The caller already treats a hook error as\nnon-fatal, so the rest of setup still succeeds.\n\n- **Verified by:** script section 3 (`TestInstallPreEditHook*`), plus section\n  7's home-folder check.\n\n### 10. The detached worker re-exec'd the test binary, 34 processes deep\n\n`launchDetachedSelf` re-execs `os.Executable()`. Under `go test` that is the\npackage's test binary, which treats `memory worker --once` as positional\narguments and **re-runs the whole package** — reaching the launcher again. Round\n1 saw 34 chained binaries, one more every 15-75 s, outliving the run, timing the\npackage out at ten minutes (it passes in 376 s without them), and re-running the\nsuite in the wrong repository, which is what wrote into the home folder.\n\nNow refuses under `go test`, detected by binary name **and** the `test.v` flag,\nbecause either signal alone can be absent. Uses package `flag` rather than\n`testing.Testing()` so the testing package stays out of the shipped binary.\n\n- **Verified by:** script section 3 and section 7's stray-process count.\n\n### 11. 32 tests failed instead of skipping without symlink privilege\n\nWindows refuses `os.Symlink` for an unprivileged account without Developer Mode.\n`internal/agentsetup` already had the right idiom and did not apply it in its\nhelper; `internal/cli` had no helper at all. Both now probe and skip on a\nprivilege refusal, and fail loudly for any other error.\n\nDeliberately **not** a blanket `runtime.GOOS == \"windows\"` skip: Developer Mode,\nan elevated shell and the CI runners all provide symlinks, and Windows is where\nthese `os.Root` semantics most need covering.\n\n- **Verified by:** section 6. Expect **skips**, not failures.\n\n### 12. The repository cannot be cloned without `core.longpaths`\n\n13 tracked files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/` reach 215 characters;\n`git clone` fails with `Filename too long`. Measured: at a 48-character clone\nroot all 13 are over 260, and only a very short root clears them.\n\nDocumented in CONTRIBUTING.md rather than fixed — renaming committed benchmark\nevidence belongs in its own change. **This is a deliberate non-fix.**\n\n### Still open\n\n`TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and\n`TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failed on both the fix and\n`baseline`. Cause undetermined; nothing in this round addresses it.\n\n---\n\n## Evidence that already exists (macOS, so: weaker)\n\n- full module suite **42 packages ok, 0 failures**\n- `gofmt -l -s` clean; `go vet` clean for host **and** `GOOS=windows` (which\n  compiles the Windows-only test files)\n- builds clean for windows/amd64, windows/arm64, linux/arm64, darwin/arm64\n- **four guards verified by weakening** — each was removed, the test confirmed\n  to go red naming the cause, and the guard restored. One first attempt produced\n  a *build* failure rather than a test failure, which proves nothing, and was\n  redone so the defect compiled.\n\nNone of that touches the behaviours in sections 1-3 of the protocol. That is\nwhat you are for.\nEOF\ncp /Users/suhaan/devenv/windows-verify.ps1 /dev/null 2>/dev/null || true\necho \"CHANGES.md: $(wc -l < \"$KIT/CHANGES.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the round-2 changes document"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4232,"cache_read_input_tokens":301754,"output_tokens":3477,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4232,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3477,"cache_read_input_tokens":301754,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4232},"type":"message"}],"speed":"s