val/bench developer-harness tests in the","+          # nightly suite (COR-2322); the shipped binary below stays untagged.","           $pkgs = (go list ./...) | Where-Object { $_ -notmatch '/internal/cli$' }","-          go test -timeout 20m $pkgs","+          go test -tags brain_harness -timeout 20m $pkgs","           if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }","-          go test -c -o \"$env:RUNNER_TEMP/cli.test.exe\" ./internal/cli","+          go test -tags brain_harness -c -o \"$env:RUNNER_TEMP/cli.test.exe\" ./internal/cli","           if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }","           Push-Location internal/cli","           # Quoted and =-joined: pwsh splits a bare -test.timeout=25m at the dot,"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/.github/workflows/test.yml","hunks":[{"oldStart":40,"oldLines":6,"newStart":40,"newLines":8,"lines":["       - uses: actions/setup-go@90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af # Official current-main v7.0.0 bundle with the repeated-DOCTYPE parser fix.","         with: { go-version: \"1.27.3\" }","       - run: go vet ./...","+      - name: Release build omits the eval/bench harnesses (COR-2322)","+        run: go test ./internal/cli -count=1 -run TestReleaseBuildOmitsHarnessCommands","       - name: Test browser controller request lifetimes","         run: node --test webui/tests/*.test.cjs","       - run: |"]},{"oldStart":119,"oldLines":6,"newStart":121,"newLines":10,"lines":["       - uses: actions/setup-go@90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af","         with: { go-version: \"1.27.3\" }","       - name: Test with race detection, coverage, and CLI contracts","+        # brain_harness compiles the eval/bench developer harnesses (COR-2322)","+        # so their tests keep running; release builds stay untagged.","+        env:","+          GOFLAGS: -tags=brain_harness","         run: go run ./tools/coverage -race -output \"${{ runner.temp }}/brain-coverage\"","       - name: Retain coverage and test results","         if: always()"]},{"oldStart":142,"oldLines":7,"newStart":148,"newLines":7,"lines":["         uses: actions/checkout@v7","         with:","           repository: entireio/entire-graph","-          ref: 28382d8ee2f0cb4ebc962255a3d8cbd364d2f258","+          ref: 3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d","           path: .context/integration-graph","           persist-credentials: false","       - name: Build both real products"]},{"oldStart":172,"oldLines":8,"newStart":178,"newLines":10,"lines":["         with: { go-version: \"1.27.3\" }","       - name: Vet every Windows package with race settings","         if: matrix.shard == 0","-        run: go vet -race ./...","+        run: go vet -tags brain_harness -race ./...","       - name: Run assigned tests with race detection and coverage","+        env:","+          GOFLAGS: -tags=brain_harness","         run: go run ./tools/coverage -race -cli-shards 6 -cli-shard ${{ matrix.shard }} -test-timeout 20m -output \"${{ runner.temp }}/brain-coverage\"","       - name: Retain test evidence","         if: always()"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":6,"newStart":63,"newLines":10,"lines":["   compact transcripts with the CLI's own `transcript` package","   (`github.com/entireio/cli` v0.13.1), whose module requires it. The source","   installer's Go check compares the patch version too (#607).","+- Say that global memories stay on the machine that recorded them.","+  `memories sync` reports how many it did not upload (`global_not_synced` in","+  JSON), and `memories global` and `remember --global` name the limit. Global","+  memories are still not synced across machines (#570)."," "," ### Fixed"," "]},{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":6,"newStart":91,"newLines":9,"lines":["   files the session's checkpoint touched) so it links to the file's symbols.","   The indexer version moves, so the next refresh re-indexes existing","   sessions (#600).","+- The pattern corpus works out a Codex session's repository root from the","+  same edit records it stores file refs from, so the two can no longer","+  disagree about which records are edits."," - `recall --evidence` no longer returns harness-injected `<system-reminder>`","   text as `role: \"user\"` evidence. User-role strings and text blocks now go","   through the same wrapper filter as the conversation reader, so reminders,"]},{"oldStart":113,"oldLines":6,"newStart":120,"newLines":23,"lines":["   codes the same way native codex records do. A patch-only turn is no longer","   classified read-only, and a failing command is no longer stored as a","   success (#566, #567).","+- Claude Code child processes that Brain starts no longer run your Claude","+  Code plugins and hooks. This covers distill, reconcile, `remember`","+  classification, memory abstracts, seed synthesis, the eval judge, query","+  expansion, outline, patterns and skills. Before, a session-memory plugin's","+  SessionStart context reached every extraction prompt, and its Stop and","+  SessionEnd hooks recorded each call as a new session. Every claude child now","+  gets `--settings '{\"disableAllHooks\":true}'`, which works on every supported","+  Claude Code version, and `CLAUDE_CODE_SAFE_MODE=1`, which on Claude Code","+  2.1.169 or later also leaves out plugins and your global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.","+  Signed-in (OAuth) auth and the `model`, `env` and `apiKeyHelper` values in","+  your user settings still apply. `--agent command` is unchanged (#552).","+","+- `remember --path` rejects a malformed path even when another path in the list","+  is valid. Previously it was dropped and the memory was stored under fewer","+  paths. The error names the rejected path and the rule: `category.subcategory.type`,","+  lowercase letters, digits and `_`, no hyphens. `remember --help` and the agent","+  guide written by `setup` now state the rule too."," "," ## [0.5.1] - 2026-11-04"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":79,"oldLines":27,"newStart":79,"newLines":6,"lines":[" the Windows CLI suite into six groups and verifies complete test results."," Required checks also include real Brain–Graph integration and repository publication checks."," ","-#### Cloning on Windows needs `core.longpaths`","-","-Thirteen tracked files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/` have relative","-paths long enough that a stock Git for Windows cannot check them out: the","-longest is 215 characters, and classic Win32 caps a path at 260 **including**","-the clone root. `git clone` fails with `Filename too long`.","-","-```sh","-git clone -c core.longpaths=true https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain","-```","-","-Or set it globally once, `git config --global core.longpaths true`. Either makes","-Git use the extended-length API; neither needs administrator rights, unlike the","-machine-wide `LongPathsEnabled` policy.","-","-A short clone root is not a reliable workaround. At a 48-character root all 13","-paths are over the limit; only a very short root such as `C:\\b` clears them, and","-nothing stops the next evidence directory from being longer. See","-[docs/limits.md](docs/limits.md#windows-path-length) for the related ceiling on","-the brain's own export tree, which is a separate limit with a separate cause.","-"," See the [development reference](docs/reference.md#development) for mise tasks"," and [installation options](docs/operations.md#local-install-brain-only) for local builds."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":149,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/.entire/agent-guide.md","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/.github/workflows/nightly.yml","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/.github/workflows/test.yml","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/CHANGELOG.md","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/CONTRIBUTING.md","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/README.md","/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/docs/agent-coordination.md","/Users/suhaan