{"parentUuid":"304adc82-c580-4c19-9038-b2495af0890e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d207a8dd-ee16-41d5-947b-5a940b090e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQszpaZeGUAiAvd5bnDh8s","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated 1 path from the index\nok 12 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)\n--- residual abstract refs in file? ---\n0\n0\n--- continue ---\n[detached HEAD 43da0777] test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\n 12 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 internal/cli/symlink_test.go\nRebasing (7/8)\rRebasing (8/8)\rSuccessfully rebased and updated refs/heads/win/full-support.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1fc9ac0b-92ad-4dcf-9547-500ee4c2c1b8","timestamp":"2026-11-17T22:55:33.432Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Updated 1 path from the index\nok 12 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)\n--- residual abstract refs in file? ---\n0\n0\n--- continue ---\n[detached HEAD 43da0777] test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\n 12 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 internal/cli/symlink_test.go\nRebasing (7/8)\rRebasing (8/8)\rSuccessfully rebased and updated refs/heads/win/full-support.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":79,"oldLines":6,"newStart":79,"newLines":27,"lines":[" the Windows CLI suite into six groups and verifies complete test results."," Required checks also include real Brain–Graph integration and repository publication checks."," ","+#### Cloning on Windows needs `core.longpaths`","+","+Thirteen tracked files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/` have relative","+paths long enough that a stock Git for Windows cannot check them out: the","+longest is 215 characters, and classic Win32 caps a path at 260 **including**","+the clone root. `git clone` fails with `Filename too long`.","+","+```sh","+git clone -c core.longpaths=true https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain","+```","+","+Or set it globally once, `git config --global core.longpaths true`. Either makes","+Git use the extended-length API; neither needs administrator rights, unlike the","+machine-wide `LongPathsEnabled` policy.","+","+A short clone root is not a reliable workaround. At a 48-character root all 13","+paths are over the limit; only a very short root such as `C:\\b` clears them, and","+nothing stops the next evidence directory from being longer. See","+[docs/limits.md](docs/limits.md#windows-path-length) for the related ceiling on","+the brain's own export tree, which is a separate limit with a separate cause.","+"," See the [development reference](docs/reference.md#development) for mise tasks"," and [installation options](docs/operations.md#local-install-brain-only) for local builds."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/docs/limits.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":120,"oldLines":6,"newStart":120,"newLines":13,"lines":[" - backup and sync agents, Explorer, and archive tools;"," - any script a user points at the store."," ","+That the Go half of this actually holds is measured, not reasoned: on Windows 11","+with `LongPathsEnabled` **0**, a probe going through Go's `os` package wrote and","+read back a 383-character absolute path, while PowerShell 5.1's `New-Item -Force`","+silently failed to create a 368-character directory on the same machine — no","+error, no directory. Both halves of the paragraph above are therefore confirmed:","+Brain's own I/O survives, and the tools around it do not.","+"," The margin is therefore not \"277 of 260 used\" — it is zero, and the thing"," holding it up is an implementation detail of the Go standard library. Enabling"," the `LongPathsEnabled` policy on the machine (`HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\"]},{"oldStart":129,"oldLines":6,"newStart":136,"newLines":13,"lines":[" `TestExportRelativePathStaysWithinItsBudget` pins the 277 in both directions, so"," a layout change that grows *or* shrinks it fails until this note is updated."," ","+The same ceiling bites the repository itself, and there it is confirmed rather","+than predicted: 13 tracked files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/` run to","+215 characters, and a stock `git clone` on Windows fails with `Filename too","+long` until `core.longpaths=true` is set. That is the \"git subprocesses, unless","+the repository sets `core.longpaths=true`\" bullet above, observed on real","+hardware. CONTRIBUTING.md carries the clone instructions.","+"," ## Egress threat model"," "," - No-egress mode (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`, deprecated alias"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/internal/cli/agent_wiring.go","hunks":[{"oldStart":194,"oldLines":6,"newStart":194,"newLines":23,"lines":[" "," func installPreEditHook(repoDir string) (string, bool, error) {"," \tpath := filepath.Join(repoDir, claudeSettingsDir, claudeSettingsFile)","+\t// A repository whose root IS the home directory is the one case where","+\t// \"repository settings\" and \"the user's global settings\" are the same file,","+\t// and the merge argument above stops holding: an entry added here does not","+\t// scope to this project, it runs in every Claude Code session on the machine.","+\t//","+\t// This is not hypothetical. On a Windows machine where C:\\Users\\<user> was","+\t// itself a git repository, a run resolved that as the repo root and merged a","+\t// PreToolUse hook into the user's global settings. Keeping a dotfiles","+\t// repository in the home directory is common enough that refusing is the","+\t// only safe default; the caller reports this as \"pre-edit hook not wired\"","+\t// and the rest of setup still succeeds.","+\tif home, err := os.UserHomeDir(); err == nil && isUserHomeDir(repoDir, home) {","+\t\treturn path, false, fmt.Errorf(\"%s is Claude Code's global settings file, not this \"+","+\t\t\t\"repository's: the repository root is your home directory. A hook written there would run \"+","+\t\t\t\"in every Claude Code session on this machine, for every project, so it was left alone. \"+","+\t\t\t\"Add it by hand if that is what you want\", path)","+\t}"," \t// Everything below goes through an os.Root: `.claude/settings.json` is a"," \t// repository-committed path like AGENTS.md, and a symlink there must not be"," \t// able to redirect this write outside the repository."]},{"oldStart":399,"oldLines":3,"newStart":416,"newLines":16,"lines":[" \t}"," \treturn commandInvokesEntireHook(command)"," }","+","+// isUserHomeDir reports whether repoDir and homeDir are the same directory.","+//","+// It reuses the synced-store comparison deliberately: that one is case","+// insensitive and separator independent on every OS, which is what this needs","+// too — Windows hands back %USERPROFILE% in whatever casing the profile was","+// created with, and a repository root can arrive with either separator.","+func isUserHomeDir(repoDir, homeDir string) bool {","+\tif repoDir == \"\" || homeDir == \"\" {","+\t\treturn false","+\t}","+\treturn normalizePathForCompare(repoDir) == normalizePathForCompare(homeDir)","+}"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/internal/cli/agent_wiring_home_guard_test.go","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":86,"lines":["+package cli","+","+import (","+\t\"os\"","+\t\"path/filepath\"","+\t\"testing\"","+)","+","+// A PreToolUse hook in <repo>/.claude/settings.json is project scoped — unless","+// the repository root is the home directory, where that path IS Claude Code's","+// global settings file and the hook runs in every session on the machine, for","+// every project.","+//","+// Observed, not imagined: on a Windows machine whose C:\\Users\\<user> was itself","+// a git repository, a run resolved the home directory as the repo root and","+// merged the hook into the user's global settings, where it stayed.","+func TestInstallPreEditHookRefusesToWriteTheUsersGlobalSettings(t *testing.T) {","+\thome := redirectHomeDir(t)","+","+\tpath, changed, err := installPreEditHook(home)","+\tif err == nil {","+\t\tt.Fatal(\"installing into the home directory must be refused; it just wrote the user's global settings\")","+\t}","+\tif changed {","+\t\tt.Error(\"a refused install must report no change\")","+\t}","+\tif want := filepath.Join(home, claudeSettingsDir, claudeSettingsFile); path != want {","+\t\tt.Errorf(\"path = %q, want %q so the message can name the file\", path, want)","+\t}","+\t// The refusal must be a refusal, not a report after the fact.","+\tif _, statErr := os.Stat(path); !os.IsNotExist(statErr) {","+\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s exists after a refused install: %v\", path, statErr)","+\t}","+}","+","+// The positive control. Without it, a guard that refused everything would look","+// identical to a guard that refuses the right thing.","+func TestInstallPreEditHookStillWiresAnOrdinaryRepository(t *testing.T) {","+\thome := redirectHomeDir(t)","+\trepo := filepath.Join(home, \"projects\", \"app\")","+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(repo, 0o755); err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatal(err)","+\t}","+","+\tpath, changed, err := installPreEditHook(repo)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a repository below the home directory must still be wired: %v\", err)","+\t}","+\tif !changed {","+\t\tt.Error(\"a fresh repository should have gained the hook\")","+\t}","+\tif _, err := os.Stat(path); err != nil {","+\t\tt.Errorf(\"settings file not written at %s: %v\", path, err)","+\t}","+}","+","+func TestIsUserHomeDir(t *testing.T) {","+\tt.Parallel()","+","+\tcases := []struct {","+\t\tname    string","+\t\trepoDir string","+\t\thomeDir string","+\t\twant    bool","+\t}{","+\t\t{\"identical\", \"/Users/sam\", \"/Users/sam\", true},","+\t\t{\"child is not the home\", \"/Users/sam/code\", \"/Users/sam\", false},","+\t\t{\"parent is not the home\", \"/Users\", \"/Users/sam\", false},","+\t\t{\"trailing separator\", \"/Users/sam/\", \"/Users/sam\", true},","+\t\t// Windows hands back whatever casing the profile was created with, and","+\t\t// a repo root can arrive with either separator.","+\t\t{\"windows casing differs\", `C:\\Users\\Sam`, `c:\\users\\sam`, true},","+\t\t{\"windows mixed separators\", \"C:/Users/Sam\", `C:\\Users\\Sam`, true},","+\t\t{\"windows sibling\", `C:\\Users\\Sam2`, `C:\\Users\\Sam`, false},","+\t\t{\"empty repo dir\", \"\", \"/Users/sam\", false},","+\t\t{\"empty home dir\", \"/Users/sam\", \"\", false},","+\t}","+\tfor _, tc := range cases {","+\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tt.Parallel()","+\t\t\tif got := isUserHomeDir(tc.repoDir, tc.homeDir); got != tc.want {","+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"isUserHomeDir(%q, %q) = %v, want %v\", tc.repoDir, tc.homeDir, got, tc.want)","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/internal/cli/memory_hardening_test.go","hunks":[{"oldStart":218,"oldLines":182,"newStart":218,"newLines":6,"lines":[" \t}"," }"," ","-<<<<<<< HEAD","-=======","-func TestMemoryMigrationInventoryRejectsAbstractDirectoryAlias(t *testing.T) {","-\tbrainDir := t.TempDir()","-\toutside := t.TempDir()","-\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(filepath.Join(brainDir, filepath.FromSlash(abstractsDirRel))), 0o700); err != nil {","-\t\tt.Fatal(err)","-\t}","-\tif err := os.Symlink(outside, filepath.Join(brainDir, filepath.FromSlash(abstractsDirRel))); err != nil {","-\t\tt.Skipf(\"symlink unavailable: %v\", err)","-\t}","-\tfindings := detectMemoryMigrations(brainDir, nil)","-\tfound := false","-\tfor _, finding := range findings {","-\t\tfound = found || finding.Path == abstractsDirRel && finding.State == brainstore.StateUnsafeCode","-\t}","-\tif !found {","-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unsafe abstract directory missing from migration findings: %+v\", findings)","-\t}","-}","-","-func validAbstractForView(view conversationSessionView, digest string) sessionAbstract {","-\tnow := time.D