achman"}
{"parentUuid":"b199d6e5-d5e1-45b2-9268-00f779b75293","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d207a8dd-ee16-41d5-947b-5a940b090e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCRc2oXeUrRK7kh2MPU1Cn","type":"tool_result","content":"=== CLASS F2: separator normalisation followed by filepath (OS-dependent compare) ===\n--- files that both ReplaceAll backslash AND call filepath.Clean ---\ninternal/sem/provider.go\ninternal/cli/stats.go\ninternal/agentsetup/agents_test.go\ninternal/agentsetup/files.go\n\n=== CLASS P2: os.Executable re-exec ===\ncmd/graph-bench/main.go:132:\texecutable, err := os.Executable()\ninternal/gitutil/process_job_windows.go:202:\texecutable, err := os.Executable()\ninternal/cli/stats_cache.go:119:\tif executable, err := os.Executable(); err == nil {\n\n=== CLASS P3: os.Symlink in tests ===\n      48\n     156\n\n=== CLASS P1: writes to .claude/settings.json ===\ninternal/cli/hook.go:16:// agentsetup.SubagentHookCommand, which setup writes into .claude/settings.local.json.\ninternal/cli/help.go:92:\t\tlong:    \"Writes one shared operating guide and managed AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md references. Preserves repository Graph/Brain activation and the saved guidance mode. --strict saves mandatory tool-use rules for all enabled products; --normal resets to normal guidance. New repositories default to normal.\\n\\nAlso registers a Claude Code SubagentStart hook (entire graph hook claude-subagent-start) in the per-user, untracked .claude/settings.local.json, merged into existing settings and added once. Claude Code's Explore and Plan subagents do not load CLAUDE.md; the hook gives them the graph directive. --no-claude-hook skips it.\\n\\nThe Claude Code status line (entire graph statusline: this session's estimated graph tokens, never prices) is opt-in and goes in the same file. At a terminal setup asks before installing it, defaulting to no; without a terminal it installs it only with --statusline. It does not ask when ours is already installed, or when .claude/settings.local.json, .claude/settings.json or ~/.claude/settings.json already defines another: a project-local status line overrides the shared and user ones, so setup keeps that one and writes nothing. --statusline installs ours anyway, overriding a shared or user line in this repository; a status line already in settings.local.json is never replaced. A settings file that cannot be read skips the status line (not the guides) unless --statusline is given. --no-statusline skips it without reading any settings, and a skip never removes a status line installed earlier.\",\ninternal/cli/help.go:97:\t\t\t{name: \"--no-claude-hook\", desc: \"Do not register the Claude Code SubagentStart hook in .claude/settings.local.json\"},\ninternal/cli/help.go:98:\t\t\t{name: \"--statusline\", desc: \"Install the status line without asking, even when .claude/settings.json or ~/.claude/settings.json defines another (exclusive with --no-statusline)\"},\ninternal/cli/help.go:99:\t\t\t{name: \"--no-statusline\", desc: \"Do not install the Claude Code status line in .claude/settings.local.json\"},\ninternal/cli/root.go:41:\t// homeDir stands in for os.UserHomeDir when non-nil: the home whose .claude/settings.json setup\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_statusline.go:123:// InstallClaudeStatusLineChanged merges statusLine into <root>/.claude/settings.local.json.\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_statusline.go:147:// project local, project shared (<root>/.claude/settings.json), user (<configDir>/settings.json,\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_statusline.go:214:const claudeSharedSettings = \".claude/settings.json\"\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_hook.go:56:const ClaudeLocalSettings = \".claude/settings.local.json\"\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_hook.go:190:// readClaudeSettings reads .claude/settings.local.json through the repository root.\ninternal/agentsetup/claude_hook.go:201:// readRepoClaudeSettings reads one settings file under .claude (name is slash-separated and\ninternal/agentsetup/