{"parentUuid":"22474aaf-b5c7-464d-b2ed-de18dfbb095d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9PRkLJLpvCuTB37S162","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":178036,"output_tokens":2018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":178036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1886,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e01539d8-01ba-4005-a767-7a718d05ff2c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch9PRjwEtkZ8dyqcDGwwN","requestRef":"a434c510-68a3-4e5f-9f83-1c514d45511b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a4e8d04f-7a96-4b30-9d2e-b8ecfe3d06a6","timestamp":"2026-11-17T23:43:14.069Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"a4e8d04f-7a96-4b30-9d2e-b8ecfe3d06a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9PRkLJLpvCuTB37S162","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LTP3ktAoYJGExtbfpYijbD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\ncat > \"$K3/.gitignore\" <<'EOF'\n# Built by bootstrap.ps1. Real git repositories live in here; nothing in them\n# belongs to this kit.\n/work/\n\n# Results you write locally before pasting them into the report.\n/out/\n*.local.md\nEOF\n\ncat > \"$K3/README.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification kit — entire-brain and entire-graph\n\nOne job: **run the Entire client stack on real Windows hardware, fix what breaks,\nand open the pull request.** Everything was written on macOS, where none of the\nuser-facing Windows behaviour can be executed. You are the execution half.\n\n```powershell\ngit clone -c core.longpaths=true <this repo> C:\\w\ncd C:\\w\npwsh -File bootstrap.ps1        # builds work\\brain and work\\graph\npwsh -File verify-brain.ps1     # phase 1: measure, change nothing\npwsh -File verify-graph.ps1\n```\n\nThen read `TESTING.md` before you touch anything. **Phase 1 is \"change nothing\".**\nThe single most valuable thing the last Windows run produced was a clean\nmeasurement of what failed — not a fix.\n\n## What is in here\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| **`CLAUDE.md`** | standing instructions for the agent doing this. Read first. |\n| **`TESTING.md`** | the three-phase protocol: measure, fix, PR |\n| `CHANGES.md` | the entire-brain change under test, item by item, with what each test does and does not prove |\n| `GRAPH-NOTES.md` | entire-graph's Windows state: what is already covered, and the leads worth hunting |\n| `PR-WORKFLOW.md` | how to turn a fix into a pull request, and the rules on it |\n| `RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md` | the shape the report comes back in |\n| `bootstrap.ps1` | builds `work\\brain` and `work\\graph` |\n| `verify-brain.ps1` | 8 sections against `work\\brain` |\n| `verify-graph.ps1` | 6 sections against `work\\graph` |\n| `src/brain/` | entire-brain @ `984c8ed4` — the baseline tree, browsable |\n| `src/graph/` | entire-graph @ `3f632e4` — main, browsable |\n| `patches/brain/` | the 8-commit Windows change, as a patch series |\n| `verify/longpath/` | the Go long-path probe |\n\n`src/` is here so you can read and grep the code without bootstrapping, and so\nthe kit still works with no network. It is **not** what you test against —\n`bootstrap.ps1` builds real git repositories in `work\\`, because a test suite\nnested inside another repository resolves the wrong repository root.\n\n## Two modes\n\n`bootstrap.ps1` picks one and tells you which.\n\n- **CLONE** — `gh` is installed and authenticated. Real clones of\n  `entireio/entire-brain` and `entireio/entire-graph`, with the brain fix branch\n  applied on top. **This is the mode that can open a pull request.**\n- **OFFLINE** — no `gh`. Repositories are built from `src/`. Everything runs;\n  nothing can be pushed. You hand back a patch instead.\n\nIf you want the PR path and bootstrap chose OFFLINE: `winget install GitHub.cli`,\n`gh auth login`, then `pwsh -File bootstrap.ps1 -Force`.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- **Go 1.27+**, native Windows (not WSL). `go env GOOS` must say `windows`.\n- **Git for Windows.** entire-brain needs `core.longpaths` to check out at all —\n  13 tracked files have paths over 200 characters against a 260 limit that\n  counts your clone root. `bootstrap.ps1` passes the flag; a clone you make by\n  hand needs `-c core.longpaths=true`.\n- **A C compiler, for entire-graph only.** Graph's tree-sitter grammars are\n  cgo. `CGO_ENABLED=0` does not build: the grammar packages are excluded and\n  the whole binary fails. Install mingw-w64 (`winget install -e --id MSYS2.MSYS2`,\n  or `choco install mingw`) and make sure `gcc --version` works. **brain needs\n  none of this** — it is pure Go, `modernc.org/sqlite` included.\n- **PowerShell.** `pwsh` 7 preferred; the scripts are written to run under\n  Windows PowerShell 5.1 too.\n- Optional: the host `entire` CLI on PATH. Two checks are weaker without it and\n  say so when they are.\n\n## What this kit is not\n\nIt has no upstream relationship to `entireio/entire-brain`. `src/` is a flat\nexport and `work\\` is yours. The only thing here that is allowed to reach\nGitHub is a pull request you open deliberately, from `work\\brain` or\n`work\\graph`, following `PR-WORKFLOW.md`.\nEOF\necho \"README.md $(wc -l < \"$K3/README.md\") lines; .gitignore ok\"","description":"Write kit README and gitignore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":178036,"output_tokens":2018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":178036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":24297,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LTP3ktAoYJGExtbfpYijbD":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\ncat > \"$K3/.gitignore\" <<'EOF'\n# Built by bootstrap.ps1. Real git repositories live in here; nothing in them\n# belongs to this kit.\n/work/\n\n# Results you write locally before pasting them into the report.\n/out/\n*.local.md\nEOF\n\ncat > \"$K3/README.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification k