h`. Confirm:\n\n```powershell\ncd work\\brain\ngit log --oneline baseline..fix-tip     # exactly the change: 8 commits\ngit status                              # clean\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Phase 1 — measure. Change nothing.\n\n```powershell\npwsh -File verify-brain.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath out\\brain.txt\npwsh -File verify-graph.ps1 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath out\\graph.txt\n```\n\n`PASS` / `FAIL` / `WARN` / `..` per check. `..` is information, `WARN` is\ncontext about your machine, only `FAIL` counts.\n\n**Save `out\\` before you edit anything.** Once you start fixing, the\nmeasurement is gone and cannot be recovered.\n\n### What each brain section proves, and what it does not\n\n- **B0 preflight.** Records whether a git repository encloses your temp or home\n  directory — round 1 ran on a machine where `C:\\Users\\<user>` was itself a\n  repo, which changed many results and caused real damage. Snapshots the real\n  store so B7 can tell what this run created.\n- **B1 store path.** A standalone `entire-brain.exe` used to read a different,\n  empty store from the host CLI's, silently. **Strong check only with the host\n  CLI present**; without it the fallback merely confirms the path is under\n  `%LOCALAPPDATA%` — necessary, not sufficient.\n- **B2 `ProcessAlive`.** Windows-only tests that have never run anywhere but a\n  Windows runner. A finished backfill used to report as running forever.\n- **B3 the known defects.** Runs by name the tests that failed on the fix and\n  passed on `baseline`, plus the five new guards. **A FAIL here means a fix for\n  a known defect did not work on Windows.** This is the section the round\n  exists for.\n- **B4 long paths, through Go.** Round 1's probe used PowerShell, whose\n  `New-Item -Force` silently fails at ~368 characters — no exception, no\n  directory. That measured PowerShell. Brain's exporter goes through Go's `os`\n  package, which rewrites long absolute paths to `\\\\?\\` first. A **PASS with\n  `LongPathsEnabled` = 0** is the informative result: the margin is zero and a\n  Go implementation detail is the only thing holding it up.\n- **B5 the repo's own path lengths.** Informational; confirms P4 still holds.\n- **B6 full suite.** `go test ./... -count=1`, with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`\n  set so repo discovery cannot walk out of a temp dir into an enclosing\n  repository — round 1 showed that walk starting a self-replicating chain of\n  test binaries.\n- **B7 what the run left behind.** Stray test binaries, and the real store\n  against B0's snapshot. **A FAIL here means the sandbox escape is back.**\n\n### What each graph section proves\n\n`GRAPH-NOTES.md` has the detail. In short: G0 toolchain (including whether cgo\nworks at all on this machine), G1 build and vet, G2 the Windows-only test files,\nG3 the full suite, G4 symlink-privilege behaviour across 48 test files, G5 real\npaths and the installed-plugin location, G6 leftovers.\n\n### Then classify every failure\n\n```powershell\ncd work\\brain\ngit checkout baseline\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TheFailingTest' -count=1\ngit checkout win/full-support\n```\n\n- fails on the fix, passes on `baseline` → **regression**. Highest value.\n- fails on both → **pre-existing**. Report it labelled.\n\n`-count=1` defeats the test cache. If a failure looks timing-related, re-run\nthat one package alone before calling it.\n\nGraph has no fix branch, so every graph failure is pre-existing by definition —\nbut check it against a clean `go clean -cache` run before blaming the product.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The manual check — please do this one\n\nStill unrun after two rounds, because the host CLI was not installed. It is the\nmost user-visible fix in the set.\n\n```powershell\n# in some git repository on this machine, NOT this kit and NOT work\\\nentire brain setup\n```\n\nThen, **while the background backfill is still running**, close the terminal\nwindow — click the X. Do not Ctrl-C, do not `exit`.\n\n1. `entire-brain.exe` should **still be running** (`Get-Process entire-brain`).\n   Before the fix it died with the console.\n2. **No console window should flash** when the backfill starts.\n\n> Deliberately **not** `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`: Microsoft documents that flag as\n> undefined in combination with `DETACHED_PROCESS`. A brief flash may be the\n> documented tradeoff rather than a bug. Report it; do not judge it.\n\nIf the host CLI is not installed, say so — that is a legitimate \"not run\".\n\n---\n\n## 5. Phase 2 — fix\n\nOnly after `out\\` is saved. The rules are in `CLAUDE.md` and they come from\n`work\\brain\\CONTRIBUTING.md`, which is the project's own:\n\n- a test that **fails without the fix**, proven by reverting the behaviour while\n  keeping identifiers compiling;\n- `[build failed]` is not a failing test — grep `--- FAIL`, never `^FAIL`;\n- the real output of the defect before, and after;\n- one commit per defect, `fix(windows): ...`, no AI attribution footers.\n\nRe-run the verify script for that repo when you are done, and re-run the full\nsuite. Then `gofmt -l -s .` — **test that its output is empty**, do not trust\nits exit code, which is 0 even when it lists files.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Phase 3 — the PR\n\n`PR-WORKFLOW.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Known-open — do not re-diagnose unless you want to\n\n`TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and\n`TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failed on both the fix and\n`baseline` in round 1, in the `bare_repository` / `not_a_repository` subtests.\nThe cause was never determined and nothing this round addresses it. If they\nstill fail, that is expected. If you see **why**, that is the bonus finding of\nthe round — and now you can fix it.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Things that are **not** bugs\n\n- `..` and `WARN` lines. Only `FAIL` counts.\n- \"host `entire` CLI not on PATH\" — expected if you did not install it.\n- \"profile is not OneDrive-redirected\" — expected on most machines. The\n  OneDrive path then gets unit coverage only, not a live store.\n- B4 passing with `LongPathsEnabled` empty or 0 — that is the expected result.\n- Tests **skipping** with \"symlinks unavailable on this host\". That is P3\n  fixed; round 1 had 32 of these as failures.\n- Graph skipping tests that need directory symlinks — graph already handles\n  this in several places and it is deliberate.\n- Capture hooks doing nothing in OFFLINE mode — `bootstrap.ps1` disables them\n  so a throwaway repo cannot attribute checkpoints somewhere wrong.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Report back\n\nFill in `RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md`. It must carry:\n\n1. Windows version, `go version`, `gcc --version`, `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion`,\n   bootstrap mode, whether the host `entire` CLI was present, whether a repo\n   encloses your home or temp directory.\n2. Both scripts' **full output**, verbatim.\n3. Per section: PASS / FAIL / NOT RUN, with exact text for anything but PASS.\n4. The manual detached-backfill result.\n5. Every suite failure attributed: pre-existing or regression.\n6. What you fixed, with the failing-test output that proves each fix.\n7. PR links, or why there is no PR.\n8. Anything you could not do, and why.\n\n**Do not round a partial result up.** \"B1 ran only its weaker half\" is a useful\nreport. \"B1 passed\" implies a comparison that never happened.\nEOF\necho \"TESTING.md $(wc -l < \"$K3/TESTING.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the round-3 testing protocol"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fe872942-ada9-4ee4-92f2-a6fa998b4f5b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9PXFCWhsTX2PaJCUuKy","requestRef":"fe5b649d-ffa4-454b-b030-4c4518496c83","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"77adf921-b845-4eda-af84-90ff819bf0ae","timestamp":"2026-11-17T23:45:17.928Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-275