 (windows-latest)\" is a\n  # required check on main. It also runs the verifier itself rather than waiting\n  # for a separate verify job, which saves one runner start at the end of the\n  # critical path. The verifier runs whenever the plan exists, so a failed shard\n  # still gets a coverage report; the last step then requires every component.\n  windows-test:\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"26782b8b-d4e6-458c-ad95-8aff937c4591","timestamp":"2026-11-17T23:45:58.526Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== lint job ===\n  lint:\n    runs-on: depot-ubuntu-24.04-4\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7.0.1\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@v7.0.0\n        with: { go-version: \"1.27.x\" }\n      - run: go vet ./...\n      - run: |\n          unformatted=$(gofmt -l -s .)\n          if [ -n \"$unformatted\" ]; then\n            echo \"::error::unformatted files:\"\n            echo \"$unformatted\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n      # Go 1.27 enables the jsonv2 experiment by default, so every other job compiles the\n      # streaming cache encoder (cache_encode_jsonv2.go) and\n      # TestDefaultBuildCompilesStreamingCacheEncoder fails if one ever does not. This step\n      # keeps the buffering fallback (cache_encode_legacy.go) compiled and byte-identical.\n      - name: cache encoder fallback (GOEXPERIMENT=nojsonv2)\n        env: { GOEXPERIMENT: nojsonv2 }\n        run: go test -count=1 -run 'Cache|EncodeCacheValue' ./internal/sem\n\n  # Release archives are immutable once published, so third-party attribution\n  # has to be correct before a tag, not after it. This regenerates NOTICES from\n  # the vendored license files and the resolved module graph and fails on any\n  # drift.\n  notices:\n\n=== windows-test-vet leg ===\n  windows-test-vet:\n    name: test (windows-latest) / vet\n    runs-on: windows-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/ch