{"parentUuid":"b77538c9-0a06-4e84-a90b-3e9eb0be4218","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9PiavjWXjqJyERc6WLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NDmvVLpbcu5zFvruNEUetM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\nK2=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncp \"$K2/CHANGES.md\" \"$K3/CHANGES.md\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3/CHANGES.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\n\nhead_old = \"\"\"# What is under test\n\n`git diff baseline..fix-tip` is exactly this and nothing else. `HEAD` carries\none further commit holding only this kit's own files.\n\nEight commits: two from round 1 (the original Windows fix), six added after a\nreal Windows machine found what the first pass could not.\n\"\"\"\nhead_new = \"\"\"# What is under test — entire-brain\n\n`git diff baseline..fix-tip` in `work\\\\brain` is exactly this and nothing else.\nThe same eight commits are in `patches/brain/` as a patch series.\n\nEight commits: two from round 1 (the original Windows fix), six added after a\nreal Windows machine found what the first pass could not.\n\n## Rebased since round 2\n\nThe branch was **64 commits behind `origin/main`** and would not have merged.\nIt is now rebased onto `984c8ed4`, which is the `baseline` tag.\n\nOne conflict, worth knowing about because it deleted code:\n`ca10da34 feat(brain)!: remove the disabled session-abstracts feature` removed\n`internal/cli/memory_abstract_hardening_test.go` upstream, and this branch had\nmodified it (a symlink-helper conversion, fix 11 below). **The resolution took\nthe upstream removal** — the symbols that test used no longer exist, so keeping\nit would not have compiled. The same commit deleted the region of\n`memory_hardening_test.go` that carried the branch's only other change to that\nfile. Nothing from the Windows work was lost; if you think otherwise, say so.\n\nOn the rebased tree, on macOS: full suite **42 packages ok**, `gofmt -l -s`\nclean, `go vet` clean for host and `GOOS=windows`, four cross-builds clean.\n\"\"\"\nassert head_old in s\ns = s.replace(head_old, head_new)\n\nfor a,b in [\n    (\"script section 1 (needs Windows)\", \"script section **B1** (needs Windows)\"),\n    (\"script section 2.\", \"script section **B2**.\"),\n    (\"script section 3, and section 7's\", \"script section **B3**, and **B7**'s\"),\n    (\"script section 3 (`TestInstallPreEditHook*`), plus section\\n7's\", \"script section **B3** (`TestInstallPreEditHook*`), plus **B7**'s\"),\n    (\"script section 3 and section 7's stray-process count\", \"script section **B3** and **B7**'s stray-process count\"),\n    (\"Verified by:** script section 3.\\n\", \"Verified by:** script section **B3**.\\n\"),\n    (\"Verified by:** section 6. Expect\", \"Verified by:** section **B6**. Expect\"),\n    (\"the manual check in TESTING.md §5\", \"the manual check in TESTING.md §4\"),\n    (\"sections 1-3 of the protocol\", \"sections B1-B3 of the protocol\"),\n]:\n    if a in s: s = s.replace(a,b)\n\ntail_old = \"\"\"None of that touches the behaviours in sections B1-B3 of the protocol. That is\nwhat you are for.\"\"\"\ntail_new = \"\"\"None of that touches the behaviours in sections B1-B3 of the protocol. That is\nwhat you are for.\n\n## What is still unverified anywhere, by anyone\n\nSay so in the report rather than letting a green run imply otherwise:\n\n- the **manual detached backfill** (fix 2) — needs the host CLI installed\n- the **strong** store-path comparison (fix 1) — same\n- the **atomic-replace retry** (fix 5) — nothing reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`\n- the **windows/arm64 CI leg** (fix 6) — only a CI run proves it, which means\n  only the PR proves it\"\"\"\nassert tail_old in s\ns = s.replace(tail_old, tail_new)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"CHANGES.md updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c . \"$K3/CHANGES.md\"","description":"Adapt CHANGES.md for round 3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3499,"cache_read_input_tokens":201114,"output_tokens":1753,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":143},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3499,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1753,"cache_read_input_tokens":201114,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3499},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":20106,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NDmvVLpbcu5zFvruNEUetM":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\nK2=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncp \"$K2/CHANGES.md\" \"$K3/CHANGES.md\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3/CHANGES.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\n\nhead_old = \"\"\"# What is under test\n\n`git diff baseline..fix-tip` is exactly this and nothing else. `HEAD` carries\none further commit holding only this kit's own files.\n\nEight commits: two from round 1 (the original Windows fix), six added after a\nreal Windows machine found what the first pass could not.\n\"\"\"\nhead_new = \"\"\"# What is under test — entire-brain\n\n`git diff baseline..fix-tip` in `work\\\\brain` is exactly this and nothing else.\nThe same eight commits are in `patches/brain/` as a patch series.\n\nEight commits: two from round 1 (the original Windows fix), six added after a\nreal Windows machine found what the first pass could not.\n\n## Rebased since round 2\n\nThe branch was **64 commits behind `origin/main`** and would not have merged.\nIt is now rebased onto `984c8ed4`, which is the `baseline` tag.\n\nOne conflict, worth knowing about because it deleted code:\n`ca10da34 feat(brain)!: remove the disabled session-abstracts feature` removed\n`internal/cli/memory_abstract_hardening_test.go` upstream, and this branch had\nmodified it (a symlink-helper conversion, fix 11 below). **The resolution took\nthe upstream removal** — the symbols that test used no longer exist, so keeping\nit would not have compiled. The same commit deleted the region of\n`memory_hardening_test.go` that carried the branch's only other change to that\nfile. Nothing from the Windows work was lost; if you think otherwise, say so.\n\nOn the rebased tree, on macOS: full suite **42 packages ok**, `gofmt -l -s`\nclean, `go vet` clean for host and `GOOS=windows`, four cross-builds clean.\n\"\"\"\nassert head_old in s\ns = s.replace(head_old, head_new)\n\nfor a,b in [\n    (\"script section 1 (needs Windows)\", \"script section **B1** (needs Windows)\"),\n    (\"script section 2.\", \"script section **B2**.\"),\n    (\"script section 3, and section 7's\", \"script section **B3**, and **B7**'s\"),\n    (\"script section 3 (`TestInstallPreEditHook*`), plus section\\n7's\", \"script section **B3** (`TestInstallPreEditHook*`), plus **B7**'s\"),\n    (\"script section 3 and section 7's stray-process count\", \"script section **B3** and **B7**'s stray-process count\"),\n    (\"Verified by:** script section 3.\\n\", \"Verified by:** script section **B3**.\\n\"),\n    (\"Verified by:** section 6. Expect\", \"Verified by:** section **B6**. Expect\"),\n    (\"the manual check in TESTING.md §5\", \"the manual check in TESTING.md §4\"),\n    (\"sections 1-3 of the protocol\", \"sections B1-B3 of the protocol\"),\n]:\n    if a in s: s = s.replace(a,b)\n\ntail_old = \"\"\"None of that touches the behaviours in sections B1-B3 of the protocol. That is\nwhat you are for.\"\"\"\ntail_new = \"\"\"None of that touches the behaviours in sections B1-B3 of the protocol. That is\nwhat you are for.\n\n## What is still unverified anywhere, by anyone\n\nSay so in the report rather than letting a green run imply otherwise:\n\n- the **manual detached backfill** (fix 2) — needs the host CLI installed\n- the **strong** store-path comparison (fix 1) — same\n- the **atomic-replace retry** (fix 5) — nothing reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`\n- the **windows/arm64 CI leg** (fix 6) — only a CI run proves it, which means\n  only the PR proves it\"\"\"\nassert tail_old in s\ns = s.replace(tail_old, tail_new)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"CHANGES.md updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c . \"$K3/CHANGES.md\"","description":"Adapt CHANGES.md for round 3"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8f0a7175-be0e-4d5a-99a8-941524817b17","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9PiahLpm5iyfB1oRGub","requestRef":"c9356c03-e10f-472c-8f89-967292d3190a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a18416fc-6a83-4cfa-b782-72510974e76b","timestamp":"2026-11-17T23:47:22.912Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
