{"parentUuid":"56af5e12-93c3-4d65-aeb5-14cd5d2883ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9PkK44EsETr6k63y3A3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187SygZeUPFiy2dPAZpS9uX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\ncat > \"$K3/PR-WORKFLOW.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Phase 3 — opening the pull request\n\nOnly after phase 1 is saved in `out\\` and phase 2's fixes each have a test that\nfails without them. If either is not true, go back; a PR is the wrong place to\ndiscover that.\n\n## The rules, which do not bend\n\n- **Draft PR.** Every one, both repos.\n- **Feature branch only.** Never commit to, push to, or force-push `main`.\n- **Never merge. Never approve. Never close anything** — not your PR, not\n  anyone else's, not an issue it fixes.\n- **Never force-push a branch you did not create.**\n- **No AI attribution footers** in commit messages or the PR body. No links to\n  agent sessions, no \"as discussed\", no references to people or conversations.\n  The commit and the PR stand on their technical content.\n- **`entireio/entire-graph` belongs to another maintainer's lane.** You may open\n  a draft PR against it. Say in the body that it came out of a Windows\n  verification run and needs that owner's review before anything else happens\n  to it. Do not touch its existing branches or PRs.\n\n## brain\n\nThe branch is already built by `bootstrap.ps1` as `win/full-support` in\n`work\\brain`, eight commits over `984c8ed4`.\n\n```powershell\ncd work\\brain\ngit fetch origin\ngit rebase origin/main          # it will have moved; expect this\ngo test ./... -count=1          # after any rebase, re-run. A rebase is a change.\n```\n\nIf the rebase conflicts: resolve it the way a maintainer would, not the way\nthat makes it build. **`--ours` can silently retire a decision upstream made on\npurpose** — that is exactly what happened when this branch was rebased in\nround 3, and taking the upstream removal was right only because upstream had\ndeliberately deleted the feature. Read the conflicting commit's message before\nchoosing a side, and say in the PR what you resolved and why.\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\ngit push -u origin win/full-support\ngh pr create --draft --repo entireio/entire-brain `\n  --base main --head win/full-support `\n  --title \"fix(windows): make the brain work on a real Windows machine\" `\n  --body-file ..\\..\\out\\brain-pr-body.md\n```\n\n**The PR's own CI is evidence you cannot get any other way.** brain's\n`windows-test` leg is a full sharded suite on a required check, and the\nwindows/arm64 build has never been tested anywhere. Wait for it, and put the\nresult in the report. If it is red, that is a finding, not a setback.\n\n## graph\n\nIf you fixed something in graph, branch off its `main`:\n\n```powershell\ncd work\\graph\ngit checkout -b win/<short-description>\n# ... commits ...\ngit push -u origin win/<short-description>\ngh pr create --draft --repo entireio/entire-graph --base main ...\n```\n\nOne PR per defect class. A PR that fixes the symlink skips and the separator\ncomparison and adds a `.gitattributes` is three reviews jammed into one.\n\n## What the PR body has to contain\n\nNot a summary — the evidence. Use this shape:\n\n```markdown\n## What this is\n\nFound by running the suite on <Windows version>, <go version>, <gcc version>,\n<admin yes/no>, <Developer Mode on/off>, <profile OneDrive-redirected yes/no>.\n\n## Each defect\n\n### <one-line title>\n\n**Reproduce, on unpatched `main`:**\n\n<paste the real failing output>\n\n**After:**\n\n<paste the passing output>\n\n**The test that fails without the fix** — `TestX` in `path/to/file_test.go`.\nProven by reverting the fix's behaviour with identifiers left compiling:\n\n<paste the --- FAIL output, which must name the cause>\n\n## Verified\n\n- [ ] full suite on Windows: <result>\n- [ ] `gofmt -l -s .` output empty\n- [ ] `go vet ./...` on Windows\n- [ ] every fix has a test that fails without it, output above\n\n## NOT verified\n\n<be specific. A gap named is worth more than a gap implied.>\n```\n\nThe last section is not a formality. `work\\brain\\CONTRIBUTING.md` says it\noutright: *a pull request that names its gaps is worth more than one that\nimplies there are none.* For this change the standing gaps are the manual\ndetached-backfill check, the `SHARING_VIOLATION` retry, and anything you could\nnot run.\n\n## If bootstrap chose OFFLINE\n\nNo PR is possible. Produce the patch series instead and hand it back:\n\n```powershell\ncd work\\brain\ngit format-patch origin/main..HEAD -o ..\\..\\out\\brain-fixes\ncd ..\\graph\ngit format-patch baseline..HEAD -o ..\\..\\out\\graph-fixes\n```\n\nThen zip `out\\` — the patches, both verify logs, and the filled-in\n`RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md` — and send that. It is the same information; someone\nelse does the pushing.\nEOF\necho \"PR-WORKFLOW.md $(wc -l < \"$K3/PR-WORKFLOW.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the PR workflow document"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1793,"cache_read_input_tokens":204613,"output_tokens":2067,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":227},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2067,"cache_read_input_tokens":204613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1793},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":27963,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0187SygZeUPFiy2dPAZpS9uX":{"command