{"parentUuid":"7bdba28e-2d95-4baa-b7bb-36b3398f3f8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9PnicCdHBZhjE7WoxjH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HqfWTyUbQC7JhfkWGCFPis","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\ncat > \"$K3/RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification — round 3 results\n\n## Machine\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Windows version | `winver` / `[System.Environment]::OSVersion.Version` |\n| Go | `go version` |\n| C compiler | `gcc --version`, or **absent** |\n| PowerShell | `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion` |\n| Administrator | yes / no |\n| Developer Mode | on / off |\n| `%USERPROFILE%` OneDrive-redirected | yes / no |\n| `LongPathsEnabled` policy | 0 / 1 / unset |\n| Host `entire` CLI on PATH | yes (version) / no |\n| A git repo encloses home or temp | yes (path) / no |\n| bootstrap mode | CLONE / OFFLINE |\n\n## Phase 1 — measurement\n\n> Paste `out\\bootstrap.txt`, `out\\brain.txt` and `out\\graph.txt` **verbatim**.\n> Not a summary. Include the lines you do not understand.\n\n<details><summary>bootstrap.txt</summary>\n\n```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>brain.txt</summary>\n\n```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>graph.txt</summary>\n\n```\n```\n</details>\n\n### brain, per section\n\n| Section | Result | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| B0 preflight | PASS / FAIL / NOT RUN | |\n| B1 store path | PASS (strong) / PASS (weak half only) / FAIL | strong needs the host CLI |\n| B2 ProcessAlive | | |\n| B3 known defects and new guards | | a FAIL here is the headline |\n| B4 long paths through Go | | note the `LongPathsEnabled` value |\n| B5 repo path lengths | informational | |\n| B6 full suite | | |\n| B7 leftovers | | a FAIL here means the sandbox escape is back |\n\n### graph, per section\n\n| Section | Result | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| G0 toolchain | | did `gcc` exist before you started? |\n| G1 build and vet | | |\n| G2 Windows-only test files | | |\n| G3 full suite | | |\n| G4 symlink privilege | | how many failed vs skipped |\n| G5 real paths, console, plugin dir | | |\n| G6 leftovers | | |\n\n### Every failure, attributed\n\n| Test | Repo | Fails on fix | Fails on baseline | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | yes/no | yes/no | regression / pre-existing |\n\n> A test that fails on both is **pre-existing** and is not this branch's fault.\n> Report it anyway, labelled.\n\n## The manual check — detached backfill\n\n- Ran it: yes / no (if no: why)\n- `entire-brain.exe` still running after the console closed: yes / no\n- Console window flashed on start: yes / no\n- Output:\n\n```\n```\n\n## Phase 2 — what you fixed\n\nFor each fix:\n\n### <title>\n\n- Repo and files:\n- Reproduction, before:\n\n```\n```\n\n- After:\n\n```\n```\n\n- Test that fails without it: `TestX` in `...`\n- Weakening proof (`--- FAIL` naming the cause):\n\n```\n```\n\n## Phase 3 — PRs\n\n| Repo | PR | State | CI |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| entire-brain | | draft | windows-test: / windows-arm64: |\n| entire-graph | | draft | |\n\nIf there is no PR, say which rule or missing tool stopped it.\n\n## What this run did to the machine\n\nRound 1 wrote `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and a `PreToolUse` hook into the user's\nhome folder and left 34 test binaries running. That report was the most useful\npart of the round. Please do the same:\n\n- Files created or modified outside the kit:\n- Processes left running:\n- Anything you had to clean up by hand:\n\n## Not run, and why\n\n> Be specific. \"B1 ran only its weaker half because the host CLI was not\n> installed\" is a useful report. \"B1 passed\" implies a comparison that never\n> happened.\n\n## Anything that looked wrong about the kit itself\n\nRound 1 found five faults in the kit and round 2 found none. Both are useful\nanswers. If a check measures the harness rather than the product — as round 1's\nPowerShell long-path probe did — that correction is worth more than a pass.\nEOF\necho \"RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md $(wc -l < \"$K3/RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md\") lines\"","description":"Write the results template"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_read_input_tokens":206406,"output_tokens":1787,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":120},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":206406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":21304,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HqfWTyUbQC7JhfkWGCFPis":{"command":"K3=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit3\ncat > \"$K3/RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Windows verification — round 3 results\n\n## Machine\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Windows version | `winver` / `[System.Environment]::OSVersion.Version` |\n| Go | `go version` |\n| C compiler | `gcc --version`, or **absent** |\n| PowerShell | `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion` |\n| Administrator | yes / no |\n| Developer Mode | on / off |\n| `%USERPROFILE%` OneDrive-redirected | yes / no |\n| `LongPathsEnabled` policy | 0 / 1 / unset |\n| Host `entire` CLI on PATH | yes (version) / no |\n| A git repo encloses home or temp | yes (path) / no |\n| bootstrap mode | CLONE / OFFLINE |\n\n## Phase 1 — measurement\n\n> Paste `out\\bootstrap.txt`, `out\\brain.txt` and `out\\graph.txt` **verbatim**.\n> Not a summary. Include the lines you do not understand.\n\n<details><summary>bootst