{"parentUuid":"e76c1a27-b3b9-4fbd-a98f-e705225f6d31","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9QCWkk7843KyhzhkK54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EZ6as7Ay9se2Sz6wfRk1gS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cd \"$S/winkit2\" || exit 1\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@entire.io\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest kit: round 3 — add entire-graph, rebase brain, hand the agent the fix and the PR\n\nRestructures the kit so the Windows machine can do the whole job rather than\njust report back.\n\n- src/brain is entire-brain at 984c8ed4 and src/graph is entire-graph at\n  3f632e4, both as plain browsable trees. Neither is what the suites run\n  against: bootstrap.ps1 builds standalone git repositories under work/,\n  because a suite nested inside another repository resolves the wrong\n  repository root.\n- The brain change is rebased onto current origin/main — it was 64 commits\n  behind — and ships as an 8-patch series. src/brain plus patches/brain\n  reconstructs the branch tip exactly (tree 96bf1a21).\n- bootstrap.ps1 picks CLONE when gh is authenticated, so the fixes land on a\n  real clone and a pull request is possible, and OFFLINE otherwise.\n- verify-brain.ps1 and verify-graph.ps1 replace windows-verify.ps1.\n- The protocol is now three phases: measure with nothing edited, then fix with\n  a test that fails without each fix, then open a draft PR. Phase 1 first is\n  the point; a green run produced by editing the thing under test is worth\n  less than a red one.\n- GRAPH-NOTES.md maps graph's Windows position: 29 _windows.go files and a\n  sharded Windows CI on a required check, so the open questions are the two\n  CI legs that exclude Windows deliberately, the absent .gitattributes, and\n  four leads carried over from the defect classes brain actually had.\n- Graph needs a C compiler on Windows and brain does not: the tree-sitter\n  grammars are cgo and CGO_ENABLED=0 excludes every grammar package.\n\nThe project README.md is no longer replaced; the kit's own lives at the root\nwhile brain's stays untouched under src/brain, which is what broke five\ndocumentation-contract tests in round 1.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1\necho \"=== size check ===\"; git count-objects -vH | grep -E 'size-pack|count'","description":"Commit the round-3 kit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":234521,"output_tokens":961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":53},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":865,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":234521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":865},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12838,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EZ6as7Ay9se2Sz6wfRk1gS":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cd \"$S/winkit2\" || exit 1\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@entire.io\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest kit: round 3 — add entire-graph, rebase brain, hand the agent the fix and the PR\n\nRestructures the kit so the Windows machine can do the whole job rather than\njust report back.\n\n- src/brain is entire-brain at 984c8ed4 and src/graph is entire-graph at\n  3f632e4, both as plain browsable trees. Neither is what the suites run\n  against: bootstrap.ps1 builds standalone git repositories under work/,\n  because a suite nested inside another repository resolves the wrong\n  repository root.\n- The brain change is rebased onto current origin/main — it was 64 commits\n  behind — and ships as an 8-patch series. src/brain plus patches/brain\n  reconstructs the branch tip exactly (tree 96bf1a21).\n- bootstrap.ps1 picks CLONE when gh is authenticated, so the fixes land on a\n  real clone and a pull request is possible, and OFFLINE otherwise.\n- verify-brain.ps1 and verify-graph.ps1 replace windows-verify.ps1.\n- The protocol is now three phases: measure with nothing edited, then fix with\n  a test that fails without each fix, then open a draft PR. Phase 1 first is\n  the point; a green run produced by editing the thing under test is worth\n  less than a red one.\n- GRAPH-NOTES.md maps graph's Windows position: 29 _windows.go files and a\n  sharded Windows CI on a required check, so the open questions are the two\n  CI legs that exclude Windows deliberately, the absent .gitattributes, and\n  four leads carried over from the defect classes brain actually had.\n- Graph needs a C compiler on Windows and brain does not: the tree-sitter\n  grammars are cgo and CGO_ENABLED=0 excludes every grammar package.\n\nThe project README.md is no longer replaced; the kit's own lives at the root\nwhile brain's stays untouched under src/brain, which is what broke five\ndocumentation-contract tests in round 1.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1\necho \"=== size check ===\"; git count-objects -vH | grep -E 'size-pack|count'","description":"Commit the round-3 kit"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4e26cebe-e9e6-4da1-8564-6c2049313545","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9QCWUcvq1eXMQ5M3YtG","requestRef":"a134ac76-f9f4-49f7-8cd4-4f489ad6ed26","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f1cfd8d-deb4-46b8-8d9c-daf52950eef5","timestamp":"2026-11-17T23:53:32.945Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2