_011ChBQSVo5pSiCDnvq7MpDs","requestRef":"8176044d-07cc-4e33-8a22-d8d9f28f31fd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0406cc88-14e2-4a3f-b943-dfcc25892a0b","timestamp":"2026-11-19T01:17:52.392Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"89d13aa3-548d-47a8-8930-2d216ba54423","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3519c29c-c027-4927-870b-4ea210ffb374","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THE7iy3kXgsN1TJHEmaj9N","type":"tool_result","content":"===== brain #654 =====\n{\"base\":\"main\",\"body\":\"## What this is\\n\\nWindows support for entire-brain, verified by running the suite on real hardware: Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200 (amd64), `go1.27.4 windows/amd64`, no C compiler (brain needs none), Windows PowerShell 5.1.26100, **not** administrator, Developer Mode **off**, profile **not** OneDrive-redirected, `LongPathsEnabled` = 0, Git for Windows 2.56.0 with `core.autocrlf=true`. The user profile `C:\\\\Users\\\\\\u003cuser\\u003e` is itself a git repository, so `%TEMP%` is inside one; that condition is what produced the two new fixes at the end of this branch.\\n\\nTen commits over `984c8ed4` (current `main`; no rebase needed):\\n\\n| Commit | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| `fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows` | data root under `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, detached backfill, `ProcessAlive`, synced-store warning, atomic-replace retry, windows/arm64 CI leg |\\n| `docs(limits): ...` | the 277-char export ceiling; narrows a lock claim |\\n| `fix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent` | the OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows |\\n| `fix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root` | tests escaped into the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` store |\\n| `fix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary` | 34 chained test binaries, suite timeout |\\n| `test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege` | 32 failures-instead-of-skips without Developer Mode |\\n| `fix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings` | repo root == home dir wrote into the user's global settings |\\n| `docs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, ...` | documented, deliberately not fixed |\\n| `fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES when finding the project root` | **new**, below |\\n| `test(cli): fence the not-a-repository degenerate case from enclosing repos` | **new**, below; closes the open `TestDegenerate*` question |\\n\\n## Verification of the first eight commits on this machine\\n\\n- Store path resolves under `%LOCALAPPDATA%` from a standalone `entire-brain.exe` with `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*_DIR` unset. **Weak half only**: the host `entire` CLI was not installed, so the standalone-vs-dispatched comparison did not run.\\n- `TestProcessAlive*` green (incl. the exited-child regression).\\n- By name, green: `TestSyncedStore*`, `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots`, `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks`, `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox`, `TestLaunchDetachedSelfRefusesUnderGoTest`, `TestMemoryWorkerLaunchAfterIsCovered`, `TestInstallPreEditHook*`, `TestIsUserHomeDir`, `TestIsSymlinkPrivilegeError`, `TestResolvePluginDataRoot*`.\\n- Long paths through Go: an export-shaped path written and read back with `LongPathsEnabled=0`.\\n- After the full suite: no stray test binaries, the real store unchanged (25 files before and after), and the home folder's `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `.claude/settings.json` byte-identical to a snapshot taken before the run.\\n- On this branch **before** the two new commits, the full suite had exactly one failure, `TestCoordinationOutsideRepository`, and it fails identically on unpatched `main`. It is pre-existing, not a regression from this change.\\n\\n## Each new defect\\n\\n### `agentsetup.Context` ignores `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`\\n\\n`Context` finds the nearest repository by walking up for `.git` \\\"without invoking Git\\\". Git honours `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`; this walk did not, so the two disagree whenever the variable is set, and the variable is set precisely to keep an enclosing repository (here, a home folder under version control) out of reach. It also means no test environment can fence this walk: the verify kit sets the ceiling for the full suite and the test still failed.\\n\\n**Reproduce, on unpatched `main`** (`GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set to the kit root, the profile and `%TEMP%`):\\n\\n```\\n=== RUN   TestCoordinationOutsideRepository\\n    coordination_test.go:171: C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1 \\u003cnil\\u003e\\n--- FAIL: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/agentsetup\\t0.548s\\n```\\n\\n`Context` returned the home folder (in its 8.3 short form, which is how `%TEMP%` is reported) for a fresh temp dir.\\n\\n**After:**\\n\\n```\\n--- PASS: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\n--- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.48s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/no_ceiling_finds_the_enclosing_repository (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_at_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_below_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/an_unrelated_ceiling_changes_nothing (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/the_starting_directory_is_still_examined (0.06s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/one_entry_of_a_list_is_enough (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.05s)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/agentsetup\\t1.040s\\n```\\n\\nEvery case is also checked against `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` with the same environment and working directory, and git agreed with all seven, including the upper-cased ceiling.\\n\\nThe comparison is **lexical**: cleaned, and case-folded on Windows. It never resolves an entry on disk, because a ceiling entry is caller-controlled and resolving one can reach a UNC path and perform network I/O (entire-graph's `resolveRepo` documents the same hazard). The trade-off is that an entry spelled differently from the walk (an 8.3 short name against the long one) does not match, which leaves the walk exactly as unfenced as it was before.\\n\\n**The test that fails without the fix:** `TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories` in `internal/agentsetup/coordination_test.go`, which does not depend on the machine having an enclosing repository. Two weakenings, identifiers left compiling.\\n\\n`isGitCeiling` made to always return false:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\n    coordination_test.go:178: C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1 \\u003cnil\\u003e\\n--- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.27s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_at_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.00s)\\n        coordination_test.go:237: Context from C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\001\\\\inner\\\\deep with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\\\\\001\\\" = \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\\\\\001\\\"; want a repository: false\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_below_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.00s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/one_entry_of_a_list_is_enough (0.00s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.00s)\\n```\\n\\nNo case folding in `comparablePath`:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.42s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.00s)\\n        coordination_test.go:237: Context from C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories1339424504\\\\001\\\\inner\\\\deep with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=\\\"C:\\\\\\\\USERS\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\APPDATA\\\\\\\\LOCAL\\\\\\\\TEMP\\\\\\\\TESTCONTEXTHONOURSGITCEILINGDIRECTORIES1339424504\\\\\\\\001\\\" = \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories1339424504\\\\\\\\001\\\"; want a repository: false\\n```\\n\\nScope: `Context`'s only caller is `entire-brain agent-guide` (a read-only preview), so the user-visible effect was a preview of the enclosing repository's guidance from a directory git says is not in one.\\n\\n### The open `TestDegenerate*` failure: the fixture was not hermetic\\n\\nEarlier Windows runs reported `TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failing on both the fix and `baseline`, cause undetermined. On this machine the cause is the enclosing repository: `not_a_repository` used a bare `t.TempDir()`, which here is inside the home-folder repository, so git answers from that repository and the condition the case names never occurs. The classifier is correct; the test's premise was false.\\n\\n**Reproduce, on unpatched `main`** (no `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`):\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText (2.29s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/not_a_repository (0.31s)\\n        degenerate_repo_test.go:72: the condition is not named:\\n            resolve HEAD for semantic index: git [-c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD]: exit status 128: fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD': unknown revision or path not in the working tree\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t9.753s\\n```\\n\\nWith `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` covering the profile and `%TEMP%`, both tests pass on unpatched `main` too. That confirms the diagnosis, and it is the change: the subtest now pins the ceiling to its temp dir's parent.\\n\\n**After** (no ambient `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`):\\n\\n```\\n--- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText (2.28s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/no_commits_yet (0.41s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/bare_repository (0.29s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/not_a_repository (0.30s)\\n--- PASS: TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository (7.32s)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t9.748s\\n```\\n\\nThis is a test-only change, so the \\\"fails without it\\\" proof is the unpatched-`main` output above, on a machine with an enclosing repository. The `bare_repository` failures reported by earlier rounds did **not** reproduce here, and this change does not claim to explain them.\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\n- [x] full suite on Windows, branch tip: **42 packages ok, 0 failures** (18 without test files) (`go test ./... -count=1`, with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set as the verify kit sets it)\\n- [x] `gofmt -l -s` output empty for the changed files, measured on the LF content git commits (see \\\"NOT verified\\\" on CRLF checkouts)\\n- [x] `go vet ./...` on Windows amd64 clean; `GOARCH=arm64 go vet ./internal/agentsetup ./internal/cli` and `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/agentsetup` clean\\n- [x] every new fix has a test that fails without it, output above\\n- [x] **again in a fresh environment**: new clone of `entire-brain` with this branch fetched in, `core.autocrlf=false`, `%TEMP%` and `GOCACHE` new and outside every repository, no `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`. Every check in the verification script passes (store path in its weaker, no-host-CLI form), the full suite is green, `gofmt -l -s .` lists nothing across the whole tree, and `go vet ./...` is clean for windows/amd64, windows/arm64 and linux/amd64\\n- [x] **the CLI end to end on Windows**, with a binary from this branch and `HOME`, `USERPROFILE`, `LOCALAPPDATA` and every `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*_DIR` sandboxed: `version`, `capabilities`, `path`, `doctor`, `setup --no-daemon --no-backfill --local-only` (18.6 s on this repository), `status`, `stats`, `overview`, `brief`, `query`, `query --keyword`, `get`, `multi-get`, `remember` → `recall` (the memory came back), `verify`, `memories status`, `agent-guide`, `refresh`, `workspace list`, `stop`/`start`, and a `bundle export` → `bundle import --sha256` round trip into an empty store, with the memory recalled from the import and a wrong checksum refused. The real home folder and real store were byte-for-byte unchanged afterwards.\\n\\n## NOT verified\\n\\n- **Anything that goes through the host `entire` CLI**, which was not installed. That covers `inspect code`, `inspect impact`, the code-index and entity-index setup components, and session export. Each failed with an exact, actionable message (`exec: \\\"entire\\\": executable file not found in %PATH%`), which is the right behaviour for a missing dependency, but the integration itself was not exercised.\\n- **The background watcher (`setup` without `--no-daemon`)** was not installed: it is a machine-wide service, and this run did not make persistent machine changes beyond the C toolchain it needed.\\n- **The detached backfill surviving a closed console** (and whether a console window flashes): needs the host `entire` CLI, which was not installed.\\n- **The strong store-path comparison** (standalone vs dispatched): same reason.\\n- **The `SHARING_VIOLATION` retry** in `internal/config/atomic_replace_windows.go`: nothing reproduces one.\\n- **The windows/arm64 CI leg**: only this PR's CI can show it.\\n- **The full suite unfenced with `%TEMP%` inside the home-folder repository** was not run, because that is the configuration that damaged a home folder in an earlier round. (Unfenced with `%TEMP%` outside any repository, it is green: the fresh-environment run above.) The two affected tests were run unfenced inside the home-folder repository, individually, above.\\n- **Symlink-dependent tests under privilege**: this account has no symlink privilege, so those tests skipped. That confirms the skip path; the symlink paths themselves were not exercised.\\n- **`gofmt -l -s .` across the tree on a stock Windows checkout lists all 1097 `.go` files**, because `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) checks them out with CRLF and `.gitattributes` does not pin `*.go` to LF. Not addressed here; it is its own change. It means `mise run test:prepush` cannot pass its gofmt step on a default Windows clone.\\n\",\"commits\":[\"fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\",\"docs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narrow a loc…\",\"fix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent\",\"fix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root\",\"fix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary\",\"test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\",\"fix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings\",\"docs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, and confirm the Go…\",\"fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES when finding the proj…\",\"test(cli): fence the not-a-repository degenerate case from enclosing …\"],\"head\":\"6e7a0b8c05d9293a969d947ea115d8e654a9a265\",\"title\":\"fix(windows): make the brain work on a real Windows machine\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5c1a6ae5-b627-49cb-881e-2e44564d8161","timestamp":"2026-11-19T01:17:53.434Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"===== brain #654 =====\n{\"base\":\"main\",\"body\":\"## What this is\\n\\nWindows support for entire-brain, verified by running the suite on real hardware: Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200 (amd64), `go1.27.4 windows/amd64`, no C compiler (brain needs none), Windows PowerShell 5.1.26100, **not** administrator, Developer Mode **off**, profile **not** OneDrive-redirected, `LongPathsEnabled` = 0, Git for Windows 2.56.0 with `core.autocrlf=true`. The user profile `C:\\\\Users\\\\\\u003cuser\\u003e` is itself a git repository, so `%TEMP%` is inside one; that condition is what produced the two new fixes at the end of this branch.\\n\\nTen commits over `984c8ed4` (current `main`; no rebase needed):\\n\\n| Commit | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| `fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows` | data root under `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, detached backfill, `ProcessAlive`, synced-store warning, atomic-replace retry, windows/arm64 CI leg |\\n| `docs(limits): ...` | the 277-char export ceiling; narrows a lock claim |\\n| `fix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent` | the OneDrive warning could never fire on Windows |\\n| `fix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root` | tests escaped into the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` store |\\n| `fix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary` | 34 chained test binaries, suite timeout |\\n| `test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege` | 32 failures-instead-of-skips without Developer Mode |\\n| `fix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings` | repo root == home dir wrote into the user's global settings |\\n| `docs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, ...` | documented, deliberately not fixed |\\n| `fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES when finding the project root` | **new**, below |\\n| `test(cli): fence the not-a-repository degenerate case from enclosing repos` | **new**, below; closes the open `TestDegenerate*` question |\\n\\n## Verification of the first eight commits on this machine\\n\\n- Store path resolves under `%LOCALAPPDATA%` from a standalone `entire-brain.exe` with `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*_DIR` unset. **Weak half only**: the host `entire` CLI was not installed, so the standalone-vs-dispatched comparison did not run.\\n- `TestProcessAlive*` green (incl. the exited-child regression).\\n- By name, green: `TestSyncedStore*`, `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots`, `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks`, `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox`, `TestLaunchDetachedSelfRefusesUnderGoTest`, `TestMemoryWorkerLaunchAfterIsCovered`, `TestInstallPreEditHook*`, `TestIsUserHomeDir`, `TestIsSymlinkPrivilegeError`, `TestResolvePluginDataRoot*`.\\n- Long paths through Go: an export-shaped path written and read back with `LongPathsEnabled=0`.\\n- After the full suite: no stray test binaries, the real store unchanged (25 files before and after), and the home folder's `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `.claude/settings.json` byte-identical to a snapshot taken before the run.\\n- On this branch **before** the two new commits, the full suite had exactly one failure, `TestCoordinationOutsideRepository`, and it fails identically on unpatched `main`. It is pre-existing, not a regression from this change.\\n\\n## Each new defect\\n\\n### `agentsetup.Context` ignores `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`\\n\\n`Context` finds the nearest repository by walking up for `.git` \\\"without invoking Git\\\". Git honours `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`; this walk did not, so the two disagree whenever the variable is set, and the variable is set precisely to keep an enclosing repository (here, a home folder under version control) out of reach. It also means no test environment can fence this walk: the verify kit sets the ceiling for the full suite and the test still failed.\\n\\n**Reproduce, on unpatched `main`** (`GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set to the kit root, the profile and `%TEMP%`):\\n\\n```\\n=== RUN   TestCoordinationOutsideRepository\\n    coordination_test.go:171: C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1 \\u003cnil\\u003e\\n--- FAIL: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/agentsetup\\t0.548s\\n```\\n\\n`Context` returned the home folder (in its 8.3 short form, which is how `%TEMP%` is reported) for a fresh temp dir.\\n\\n**After:**\\n\\n```\\n--- PASS: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\n--- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.48s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/no_ceiling_finds_the_enclosing_repository (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_at_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_below_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/an_unrelated_ceiling_changes_nothing (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/the_starting_directory_is_still_examined (0.06s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/one_entry_of_a_list_is_enough (0.05s)\\n    --- PASS: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.05s)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/agentsetup\\t1.040s\\n```\\n\\nEvery case is also checked against `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` with the same environment and working directory, and git agreed with all seven, including the upper-cased ceiling.\\n\\nThe comparison is **lexical**: cleaned, and case-folded on Windows. It never resolves an entry on disk, because a ceiling entry is caller-controlled and resolving one can reach a UNC path and perform network I/O (entire-graph's `resolveRepo` documents the same hazard). The trade-off is that an entry spelled differently from the walk (an 8.3 short name against the long one) does not match, which leaves the walk exactly as unfenced as it was before.\\n\\n**The test that fails without the fix:** `TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories` in `internal/agentsetup/coordination_test.go`, which does not depend on the machine having an enclosing repository. Two weakenings, identifiers left compiling.\\n\\n`isGitCeiling` made to always return false:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestCoordinationOutsideRepository (0.00s)\\n    coordination_test.go:178: C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1 \\u003cnil\\u003e\\n--- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.27s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_at_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.00s)\\n        coordination_test.go:237: Context from C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\001\\\\inner\\\\deep with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\\\\\001\\\" = \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories230945526\\\\\\\\001\\\"; want a repository: false\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/a_ceiling_below_the_repository_stops_the_walk (0.00s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/one_entry_of_a_list_is_enough (0.00s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.00s)\\n```\\n\\nNo case folding in `comparablePath`:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories (0.42s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories/letter_case_does_not_matter_where_the_filesystem_ignores_it (0.00s)\\n        coordination_test.go:237: Context from C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories1339424504\\\\001\\\\inner\\\\deep with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=\\\"C:\\\\\\\\USERS\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\APPDATA\\\\\\\\LOCAL\\\\\\\\TEMP\\\\\\\\TESTCONTEXTHONOURSGITCEILINGDIRECTORIES1339424504\\\\\\\\001\\\" = \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\TestContextHonoursGitCeilingDirectories1339424504\\\\\\\\001\\\"; want a repository: false\\n```\\n\\nScope: `Context`'s only caller is `entire-brain agent-guide` (a read-only preview), so the user-visible effect was a preview of the enclosing repository's guidance from a directory git says is not in one.\\n\\n### The open `TestDegenerate*` failure: the fixture was not hermetic\\n\\nEarlier Windows runs reported `TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText` and `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` failing on both the fix and `baseline`, cause undetermined. On this machine the cause is the enclosing repository: `not_a_repository` used a bare `t.TempDir()`, which here is inside the home-folder repository, so git answers from that repository and the condition the case names never occurs. The classifier is correct; the test's premise was false.\\n\\n**Reproduce, on unpatched `main`** (no `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`):\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText (2.29s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/not_a_repository (0.31s)\\n        degenerate_repo_test.go:72: the condition is not named:\\n            resolve HEAD for semantic index: git [-c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD]: exit status 128: fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD': unknown revision or path not in the working tree\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t9.753s\\n```\\n\\nWith `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` covering the profile and `%TEMP%`, both tests pass on unpatched `main` too. That confirms the diagnosis, and it is the change: the subtest now pins the ceiling to its temp dir's parent.\\n\\n**After** (no ambient `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`):\\n\\n```\\n--- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText (2.28s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/no_commits_yet (0.41s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/bare_repository (0.29s)\\n    --- PASS: TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText/not_a_repository (0.30s)\\n--- PASS: TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository (7.32s)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t9.748s\\n```\\n\\nThis is a test-only change, so the \\\"fails without it\\\" proof is the unpatched-`main` output above, on a machine with an enclosing repository. The `bare_repository` failures reported by earlier rounds did **not** reproduce here, and this change does not claim to explain them.\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\n- [x] full suite on Windows, branch tip: **42 packages ok, 0 failures** (18 without test files) (`go test ./... -count=1`, with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set as the verify kit sets it)\\n- [x] `gofmt -l -s` output empty for the changed files, measured on the LF content git commits (see \\\"NOT verified\\\" on CRLF checkouts)\\n- [x] `go vet ./...` on Windows amd64 clean; `GOARCH=arm64 go vet ./internal/agentsetup ./internal/cli` and `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/agentsetup` clean\\n- [x] every new fix has a test that fails without it, output above\\n- [x] **again in a fresh environment**: new clone of `entire-brain` with this branch fetched in, `core.autocrlf=false`, `%TEMP%` and `GOCACHE` new and outside every repository, no `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`. Every check in the verification script passes (store path in its weaker, no-host-CLI form), the full suite is green, `gofmt -l -s .` lists nothing across the whole tree, and `go vet ./...` is clean for windows/amd64, windows/arm64 and linux/amd64\\n- [x] **the CLI end to end on Windows**, with a binary from this branch and `HOME`, `USERPROFILE`, `LOCALAPPDATA` and every `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*_DIR` sandboxed: `version`, `capabilities`, `path`, `doctor`, `setup --no-daemon --no-backfill --local-only` (18.6 s on this repository), `status`, `stats`, `overview`, `brief`, `query`, `query --keyword`, `get`, `multi-get`, `remember` → `recall` (the memory came back), `verify`, `memories status`, `agent-guide`, `refresh`, `workspace list`, `stop`/`start`, and a `bundle export` → `bundle import --sha256` round trip into an empty store, with the memory recalled from the import and a wrong checksum refused. The real home folder and real store were byte-for-byte unchanged afterwards.\\n\\n## NOT verified\\n\\n- **Anything that goes through the host `entire` CLI**, which was not installed. That covers `inspect code`, `inspect impact`, the code-index and entity-index setup components, and session export. Each failed with an exact, actionable message (`exec: \\\"entire\\\": executable file not found in %PATH%`), which is the right behaviour for a missing dependency, but the integration itself was not exercised.\\n- **The background watcher (`setup` without `--no-daemon`)** was not installed: it is a machine-wide service, and this run did not make persistent machine changes beyond the C toolchain it needed.\\n- **The detached backfill surviving a closed console** (and whether a console window flashes): needs the host `entire` CLI, which was not installed.\\n- **The strong store-path comparison** (standalone vs dispatched): same reason.\\n- **The `SHARING_VIOLATION` retry** in `internal/config/atomic_replace_windows.go`: nothing reproduces one.\\n- **The windows/arm64 CI leg**: only this PR's CI can show it.\\n- **The full suite unfenced with `%TEMP%` inside the home-folder repository** was not run, because that is the configuration that damaged a home folder in an earlier round. (Unfenced with `%TEMP%` outside any repository, it is green: the fresh-environment run above.) The two affected tests were run unfenced inside the home-folder repository, individually, above.\\n- **Symlink-dependent tests under privilege**: this account has no symlink privilege, so those tests skipped. That confirms the skip path; the symlink paths themselves were not exercised.\\n- **`gofmt -l -s .` across the tree on a stock Windows checkout lists all 1097 `.go` files**, because `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) checks them out with CRLF and `.gitattributes` does not pin `*.go` to LF. Not addressed here; it is its own change. It means `mise run test:prepush` cannot pass its gofmt step on a default Windows clone.\\n\",\"commits\":[\"fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\",\"docs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narrow a loc…\",\"fix(windows): make the synced-store comparison OS-independent\",\"fix(windows): keep the test sandbox over the Windows store root\",\"fix(test): stop the detached worker re-execing the test binary\",\"test(windows): skip symlink tests when the host withholds the privilege\",\"fix(setup): refuse to write a pre-edit hook into global Claude settings\",\"docs: record the core.longpaths clone requirement, and confirm the Go…\",\"fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES when finding the proj…\",\"test(cli): fence the not-a-repository degenerate case from enclosing …\"],\"head\":\"6e7a0b8c05d9293a969d947ea115d8e654a9a265\",\"title\":\"fix(windows): make the brain work on a real Windows machine\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"99dda994-167a-4e8a-ab55-30c3cf8d9ea8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":273},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"89d13aa3-548d-47a8-8930-2d216ba54423","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
