{"parentUuid":"1cd02d64-44bd-43c3-9313-a2d2765c32b2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01UCvqRgqejkasAz8aoesYTy","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk ls -la /Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md /Users/suhaan/devenv/AGENT-COMMS.md 2>&1 | head; echo \\\"=== GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md head ===\\\"; rtk read /Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md --max-lines 25 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"=== tail ===\\\"; rtk read /Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md --tail-lines 15 2>/dev/null\",\"description\":\"Check graph feedback channel files\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":15},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2f311573-fe77-4be8-b4db-bcc3eef74207","timestamp":"2026-11-19T01:30:57.946Z","session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"0e971ba3-c5b5-4564-8afc-af295ad0acaa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81f4e51e-73e3-4088-b895-b584b771fffc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCvqRgqejkasAz8aoesYTy","type":"tool_result","content":"644  /Users/suhaan/devenv/AGENT-COMMS.md  54.5K\n644  /Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md  20.4K\n=== GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md head ===\n# entire-graph — field feedback from a long agent session\n\nWritten 2026-09-23 after a full working session in `entire-brain` (~1,800 files,\n33 code fixes). Evidence is from this repo, at `gap-scale` @ `1c56dcdf`.\n\n**The headline, and it is uncomfortable: I did not use the graph at all for the\nentire session.** Every code location came from `grep`. The repo's own\n`.entire/graph-agent.md` says *\"SEARCH FIRST — never grep/find/cat to locate\ncode before you have searched\"*, and I violated it on every lookup. That is an\nagent-compliance failure first. But when I finally did run it, the results below\nexplain why nothing pulled me back, and that part is a product problem.\n\n[384 more lines]=== tail ===\n\nBoth plausible answers sit in the same file as the decoy's caller, so this is not a\nrecall failure — the symbols were indexed. It is a ranking failure on a question phrased\nas intent rather than as a name. That is exactly the query shape the `--profile full`\npitch is aimed at.\n\n**The useful signal for graph:** winning the first call is now the easy half. An agent that\ncomplies once, gets a decoy, and falls back to grep has learned the tool does not pay —\nand it will not comply twice. Ranking on intent-phrased queries is worth more than any\nfurther wording change.\n\nCaveat on the usage half, stated plainly: the guide text was injected into each agent's\nPROMPT, not read from `.entire/agent-guide.md`. So this measures whether the wording works\nonce in context, not whether the file gets read. It cannot reproduce the 0.34% baseline and\nshould not be quoted as if it did. n=2 per arm.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2103f61e-7668-49c1-88eb-8514d6c5d5fa","timestamp":"2026-11-19T01:30:58.016Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"644  /Users/suhaan/devenv/AGENT-COMMS.md  54.5K\n644  /Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md  20.4K\n=== GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md head ===\n# entire-graph — field feedback from a long agent session\n\nWritten 2026-09-23 after a full working session in `entire-brain` (~1,800 files,\n33 code fixes). Evidence is from this repo, at `gap-scale` @ `1c56dcdf`.\n\n**The headline, and it is uncomfortable: I did not use the graph at all for the\nentire session.** Every code location came from `grep`. The repo's own\n`.entire/graph-agent.md` says *\"SEARCH FIRST — never grep/find/cat to locate\ncode before you have searched\"*, and I violated it on every lookup. That is an\nagent-compliance failure first. But when I finally did run it, the results below\nexplain why nothing pulled me back, and that part is a product problem.\n\n[384 more lines]=== tail ===\n\nBoth plausible answers sit in the same file as the decoy's caller, so this is not a\nrecall failure — the symbols were indexed. It is a ranking failure on a question phrased\nas intent rather than as a name. That is exactly the query shape the `--profile full`\npitch is aimed at.\n\n**The useful signal for graph:** winning the first call is now the easy half. An agent that\ncomplies once, gets a decoy, and falls back to grep has learned the tool does not pay —\nand it will not comply twice. Ranking on intent-phrased queries is worth more than any\nfurther wording change.\n\nCaveat on the usage half, stated plainly: the guide text was injected into each agent's\nPROMPT, not read from `.entire/agent-guide.md`. So this measures whether the wording works\nonce in context, not whether the file gets read. It cannot reproduce the 0.34% baseline and\nshould not be quoted as if it did. n=2 per arm.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext"