{"parentUuid":"de6a2b23-ecc7-4e5b-9a8f-ade94e8dec25","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011ChCyMbY5jmhYHHV6t1mDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LVGTYyLeSjYUVUeEZnC7F7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-WINDOWS-PROMPT.md","content":"# Graph lane — Windows support: review, fix, finalize\n\n> Hand this to a graph session. **Launch it from `~/devenv/entire-graph`, never from\n> `~/devenv`** — devenv carries no capture hooks, so a session rooted there records nothing\n> and says nothing about it.\n\n---\n\nFour draft PRs sit on `entireio/entire-graph` — **#416, #417, #418, #419**. They were opened\nunder the user's GitHub account by a verification agent running on real Windows hardware, not\nby a human and not by you. Your job is to review them, fix what they leave open, and bring\ngraph's Windows story to a finished state. Nothing merges until the user says so.\n\n## Before anything else\n\n- Preflight as the agent guide requires: `entire graph version --json`,\n  `entire graph capabilities --json`, `entire brain version`, then\n  `entire brain brief \"graph Windows support review\" --json`. Record the results.\n- **Read `~/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md`, the section headed\n  `## Reviewed 2026-11-18: four Windows draft PRs (#416–#419) — handoff to the graph lane`.**\n  That is the brief: per-PR verdicts, what was verified independently, and the four decisions\n  that are yours. It was written by the brain-lane session. Treat it as a peer report —\n  reproduce the claims that will change what you do, don't adopt them.\n- **Do not work in `~/devenv/entire-graph` itself.** It is at `d4a0c186`, ~226 commits behind\n  `origin/main`, with a dirty tree. Six agents have already produced confident wrong findings\n  by reading stale checkouts. Make one fresh worktree off `origin/main` per task.\n- Check `uptime` first. Graph's suite is large and the tree-sitter grammars are cgo; a full\n  local run at full parallelism competes with whatever else is on this machine.\n\n## Standing constraints — these override anything below that reads like a shipping step\n\n- **No merging, no approvals, no closing, no pushing to `main`, on any repo.** The PRs stay\n  draft. The user reviews once at the end; you report, they merge.\n- **Lanes.** You own `entire-graph`. The brain session owns `entire-brain`. Ask before\n  touching the other repo, its branches, or its open PRs.\n- **No AI attribution footers in commits** (user-level rule, overrides any harness reminder).\n  One commit per defect, conventional scope, `fix(windows): …` / `test(sem): …`.\n- Board writes (`~/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`): `\"lane\": \"graph\"` rows only, under an\n  exclusive `fcntl.flock` on `.claude/todo-board.lock`, `.tmp` then `os.replace`.\n- Never bare `git stash` / `git stash pop` — one `refs/stash` is shared across every worktree\n  and other sessions are live. Use `git stash push -u -m \"<tag>\"`, capture the SHA,\n  `git stash apply <sha>`.\n- Do not run `entire enable` in `devenv/`.\n\n## The four PRs\n\nAll four are green on every leg — ubuntu, macos (12 shards), windows-latest — and all four are\n`MERGEABLE`. The hardware they were found on: Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200 amd64, go1.27.4,\ngcc 16.2.0 MinGW-w64 UCRT, non-administrator, Developer Mode off, and a user profile that is\nitself a git repository (so `%TEMP%` sits inside one — a configuration no CI runner has, and a\ncommon one for anyone keeping dotfiles in git).\n\n| PR | Branch | Verdict carried over | What finishing it means |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **#416** `fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` | `win/agentsetup-git-ceiling` | Sound. One design question. | Decide the shared-resolver question below, then finalize. |\n| **#417** `test: skip symlink fixtures where the host withholds the privilege` | `win/agentsetup-symlink-probe` | Sound. | Decide whether `sem` gets a helper + guard too. |\n| **#418** `test(sem): skip the verify replay when sh is absent` | `win/sem-verify-test-needs-sh` | Sound, trivial (5 lines). | Confirm and finalize. |\n| **#419** `fix(sem): accept a leading UTF-8 BOM in a compact snapshot` | `win/compact-snapshot-utf8-bom` | Correct, but **does not close the flow it documents**. | See below — this one needs work, not just review. |\n\n### #419 is the one that needs fixing, not just reviewing\n\nWindows PowerShell 5.1's `>` defaults to **UTF-16LE**, not UTF-8-with-BOM. The PR's own table\nshows a UTF-8 BOM only because that machine's profile had changed the default, and its \"NOT\nverified\" section admits it. So on a stock Windows box the flow the PR documents —\n\n```\nentire graph snapshot --repo . --format compact-ndjson > graph.compact.ndjson\nentire graph snapshot-query --input graph.compact.ndjson --symbol Foo\n```\n\n— **still fails**, with a different error. Reproduce that before deciding anything.\n\nThe BOM skip is worth having on its own terms (it matches what the git-config guard and\n`agentsetup`'s Claude-settings reader already do). What's missing is one of:\n\n- the `--output <file>` flag the PR proposes and leaves to you — the change that actually\n  closes the flow; and/or\n- a clear, named error when the input is UTF-16 (BOM `FF FE` / `FE FF`), instead of whatever\n  the decoder currently says. Decoding UTF-16 is the other option; rejecting it with a message\n  that names PowerShell's default is probably the better one.\n\nEither way: take the BOM fix, **do not close the underlying issue on it**.\n\n## The work that is in no PR yet — this is most of \"finalize\"\n\n1. **graph has no `.gitattributes` at all.** With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows\n   default) a stock Windows clone checks out every `.go` file with CRLF, and `gofmt -l -s .`\n   then lists all of them — so graph's gofmt gate cannot pass on a default Windows clone, and\n   every golden fixture is unpinned for the same reason. CI cannot see this: runners check out\n   LF. The brain-lane fix is `*.go text eol=lf` plus a **class guard** (a test asserting the\n   property of every file in the class, not of the paths someone remembered). Read it rather\n   than reinvent it: `~/devenv/brain-goeol/.gitattributes` lines 1–9 and\n   `~/devenv/brain-goeol/internal/setupui/go_source_eol_test.go` (branch `win/go-eol-lf`,\n   commit `7873db4d`, **local only — not pushed**, so it is not on the remote to fetch).\n   The safety proof that a pin is checkout-only: `git add --renormalize .` must rewrite zero\n   files. Graph also needs its goldens and any byte-exact fixtures considered — check for\n   anything that must stay byte-for-byte and give it `-text` *after* the broad rule, since\n   later rules win.\n2. **Run graph's suite once on a CRLF checkout.** It never has been. `git clone -c\n   core.autocrlf=true` into a scratch dir and run it. Until that exists, nobody can say\n   whether graph's CRLF exposure is gofmt-only the way brain's is.\n3. **cgo is a Windows contributor prerequisite and is undocumented.** Every tree-sitter grammar\n   `import \"C\"` with no pure-Go fallback, so `GOOS=windows CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./...` fails\n   for all of them. Irrelevant for released binaries; a hard wall for a Windows contributor,\n   who needs mingw-w64 before the repo builds at all. Put it in the contributor docs.\n4. **Three copies of git's ceiling rule now exist across two repos**, already diverging in\n   shape: #416 adds `internal/agentsetup/gitceiling.go` (applied at two call sites) rather than\n   importing `sem`'s resolver, because `agentsetup` imports no internal package today; brain\n   landed the same logic inline in `internal/agentsetup/migration.go` in its PR #654. You and\n   brain already share the guide renderer (graph #366 / brain #447), so there is precedent for\n   sharing this. **Your call** — and if the answer is \"share\", message the brain session with\n   `SendMessage` and agree the shape before anything touches brain's repo.\n5. **`sem` symlink coverage.** #417's AST-based class guard covers `agentsetup` only. `sem` has\n   156 `os.Symlink` call sites across 48 test files with no shared helper to anchor a guard on.\n   Whether that earns a helper is your call; if you skip it, say so explicitly rather than\n   leaving it looking covered.\n\n## The verification bar\n\nFrom graph's own CONTRIBUTING.md, and it is not negotiable:\n\n- Every fix needs a test that **fails without the fix**, proven by reverting the behaviour\n  while keeping identifiers compiling. State the output before and after.\n- `[build failed]` is not a failing test. Grep `--- FAIL`, never `^FAIL`.\n- `gofmt -l -s .` — **test that its output is empty.** Its exit code is 0 even when it lists\n  files.\n- Where only a Windows runner or a real Windows box can prove something, say so and leave it\n  unproven. Do not present a bounded source check as equivalent.\n\n## When you're done\n\nReport: a verdict per PR, what you changed and on which branches, what the user has to decide\nor click, and anything you could not verify from macOS. Nothing merged, nothing pushed to\n`main`, nothing closed.\n\n## Do not\n\n- Touch `entire-brain` — its repo, its branches (`win/full-support`, `win/go-eol-lf`), or its\n  PRs (#654) — without asking the brain session first.\n- Approve, merge, close, or comment publicly on any PR.\n- Trust the stale `~/devenv/entire-graph` checkout, or any finding derived from it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":128236,"output_tokens":5410,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1812},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":687,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5410,"cache_read_input_tokens":128236,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":687},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":43499,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LVGTYyLeSjYUVUeEZnC7F7":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-WINDOWS-PROMPT.md","content":"# Graph lane — Windows support: review, fix, finalize\n\n> Hand this to a graph session. **Launch it from `~/devenv/entire-graph`, never from\n> `~/devenv`** — devenv carries no capture hooks, so a session rooted there records nothing\n> and says nothing about it.\n\n---\n\nFour draft PRs sit on `entireio/entire-graph` — **#416, #417, #418, #419**. They were opened\nunder the user's GitHub account by a verification agent running on real Windows hardware, not\nby a human and not by you. Your job is to review them, fix what they leave open, and bring\ngraph's Windows story to a finished state. Nothing merges until the user says so.\n\n## Before anything else\n\n- Preflight as the agent guide requires: `entire graph version --json`,\n  `entire graph capabilities --json`, `entire brain version`, then\n  `entire brain brief \"graph Windows support review\" --json`. Record the results.\n- **Read `~/devenv/GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md`, the section headed\n  `## Reviewed 2026-11-18: four Windows draft PRs (#416–#419) — handoff to the graph lane`.**\n  That is the brief: per-PR verdicts, what was verified independently, and the four decisions\n  that are yours. It was written by the brain-lane session. Treat it as a peer report —\n  reproduce the claims that will change what you do, don't adopt them.\n- **Do not work in `~/devenv/entire-graph` itself.** It is at `d4a0c186`, ~226 commits behind\n  `origin/main`, with a dirty tree. Six agents have already produced confident wrong findings\n  by reading stale checkouts. Make one fresh worktree off `origin/main` per task.\n- Check `uptime` first. Graph's suite is large and the tree-sitter grammars are cgo; a full\n  local run at full parallelism competes with whatever else is on this machine.\n\n## Standing constraints — these override anything below that reads like a shipping step\n\n- **No merging, no approvals, no closing, no pushing to `main`, on any repo.** The PRs stay\n  draft. The user reviews once at the end; you report, they merge.\n- **Lanes.** You own `entire-graph`. The brain session owns `entire-brain`. Ask before\n  touching the other repo, its branches, or its open PRs.\n- **No AI attribution footers in commits** (user-level rule, overrides any harness reminder).\n  One commit per defect, conventional scope, `fix(windows): …` / `test(sem): …`.\n- Board writes (`~/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`): `\"lane\": \"graph\"` rows only, under an\n  exclusive `fcntl.flock` on `.claude/todo-board.lock`, `.tmp` then `os.replace`.\n- Never bare `git stash` / `git stash pop` — one `refs/stash` is shared across every worktree\n  and other sessions are live. Use `git stash push -u -m \"<tag>\"`, capture the SHA,\n  `git stash apply <sha>`.\n- Do not run `entire enable` in `devenv/`.\n\n## The four PRs\n\nAll four are green on every leg — ubuntu, macos (12 shards), windows-latest — and all four are\n`MERGEABLE`. The hardware they were found on: Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200 amd64, go1.27.4,\ngcc 16.2.0 MinGW-w64 UCRT, non-administrator, Developer Mode off, and a user profile that is\nitself a git repository (so `%TEMP%` sits inside one — a configuration no CI runner has, and a\ncommon one for anyone keeping dotfiles in git).\n\n| PR | Branch | Verdict carried over | What finishing it means |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **#416** `fix(agentsetup): honour GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` | `win/agentsetup-git-ceiling` | Sound. One design question. | Decide the shared-resolver question below, then finalize. |\n| **#417** `test: skip symlink fixtures where the host withholds the privilege` | `win/agentsetup-symlink-probe` | Sound. | Decide whether `sem` gets a helper + guard too. |\n| **#418** `test(sem): skip the verify replay when sh is absent` | `win/sem-verify-test-needs-sh` | Sound, trivial (5 lines). | Confirm and finalize. |\n| **#419** `fix(sem): accept a leading UTF-8 BOM in a compact snapshot` | `win/compact-snapshot-utf8-bom` | Correct, but **does not close the flow it documents**. | See below — this one needs work, not just review. |\n\n### #419 is the one that needs fixing, not just reviewing\n\nWindows PowerShell 5.1's `>` defaults to **UTF-16LE**, not UTF-8-with-BOM. The PR's own table\nshows a UTF-8 BOM only because that machine's profile had changed the default, and its \"NOT\nverified\" section admits it. So on a stock Windows box the flow the PR documents —\n\n```\nentire graph snapshot --repo . --format compact-ndjson > graph.compact.ndjson\nentire graph snapshot-query --input graph.compact.ndjson --symbol Foo\n```\n\n— **still fails**, with a different error. Reproduce that before deciding anything.\n\nThe BOM skip is worth having on its own terms (it matches what the git-config guard and\n`agentsetup`'s Claude-settings reader already do). What's missing is one of:\n\n- the `--output <file>` flag the PR proposes and leaves to you — the change that actually\n  closes the flow; and/or\n- a clear, named error when the input is UTF-16 (BOM `FF FE` / `FE FF`), instead of whatever\n  the decoder currently says. Decoding UTF-16 is the other option; rejecting it with a message\n  that names PowerShell's default is probably the better one.\n\nEither way: take the BOM fix, **do not close the underlying issue on it**.\n\n## The work that is in no PR yet — this is most of \"finalize\"\n\n1. **graph has no `.gitattributes` at all.** With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows\n   default) a stock Windows clone checks out every `.go` file with CRLF, and `gofmt -l -s .`\n   then lists all of them — so graph's gofmt gate cannot pass on a default Windows clone, and\n   every golden fixture is unpinned for the same reason. CI cannot see this: runners check out\n   LF. The brain-lane fix is `*.go text eol=lf` plus a **class guard** (a test asserting the\n   property of every file in the class, not of the paths someone remembered). Read it rather\n   than reinvent it: `~/devenv/brain-goeol/.gitattributes` lines 1–9 and\n   `~/devenv/brain-goeol/internal/setupui/go_source_eol_test.go` (branch `win/go-eol-lf`,\n   commit `7873db4d`, **local only — not pushed**, so it is not on the remote to fetch).\n   The safety proof that a pin is checkout-only: `git add --renormalize .` must rewrite zero\n   files. Graph also needs its goldens and any byte-exact fixtures considered — check for\n   anything that must stay byte-for-byte and give it `-text` *after* the broad rule, since\n   later rules win.\n2. **Run graph's suite once on a CRLF checkout.** It never has been. `git clone -c\n   core.autocrlf=true` into a scratch dir and run it. Until that exists, nobody can say\n   whether graph's CRLF exposure is gofmt-only the way brain's is.\n3. **cgo is a Windows contributor prerequisite and is undocumented.** Every tree-sitter grammar\n   `import \"C\"` with no pure-Go fallback, so `GOOS=windows CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./...` fails\n   for all of them. Irrelevant for released binaries; a hard wall for a Windows contributor,\n   who needs mingw-w64 before the repo builds at all. Put it in the contributor docs.\n4. **Three copies of git's ceiling rule now exist across two repos**, already diverging in\n   shape: #416 adds `internal/agentsetup/gitceiling.go` (applied at two call sites) rather than\n   importing `sem`'s resolver, because `agentsetup` imports no internal package today; brain\n   landed the same logic inline in `internal/agentsetup/migration.go` in its PR #654. You and\n   brain already share the guide renderer (graph #366 / brain #447), so there is precedent for\n   sharing this. **Your call** — and if the answer is \"share\", message the brain session with\n   `SendMessage` and agree the shape before anything touches brain's repo.\n5. **`sem` symlink coverage.** #417's AST-based class guard covers `agentsetup` only. `sem` has\n   156 `os.Symlink` call sites across 48 test files with no shared helper to anchor a guard on.\n   Whether that earns a helper is your call; if you skip it, say so explicitly rather than\n   leaving it looking covered.\n\n## The verification bar\n\nFrom graph's own CONTRIBUTING.md, and it is not negotiable:\n\n- Every fix needs a test that **fails without the fix**, proven by reverting the behaviour\n  while keeping identifiers compiling. State the output before and after.\n- `[build failed]` is not a failing test. Grep `--- FAIL`, never `^FAIL`.\n- `gofmt -l -s .` — **test that its output is empty.** Its exit code is 0 even when it lists\n  files.\n- Where only a Windows runner or a real Windows box can prove something, say so and leave it\n  unproven. Do not present a bounded source check as equivalent.\n\n## When you're done\n\nReport: a verdict per PR, what you changed and on which branches, what the user has to decide\nor click, and anything you could not verify from macOS. Nothing merged, nothing pushed to\n`main`, nothing closed.\n\n## Do not\n\n- Touch `entire-brain` — its repo, its branches (`win/full-support`, `win/go-eol-lf`), or its\n  PRs (#654) — without asking the brain session first.\n- Approve, merge, close, or comment publicly on any PR.\n- Trust the stale `~/devenv/entire-graph` checkout, or any finding derived from it.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e38b66c5-6439-42e3-98ca-04c4ac210237","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChCyMbHwXScRaezhTYWwC","requestRef":"87d8fa9a-c18c-40d4-80e2-7c8ecf585d70","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"43c13327-a993-4614-af66-7b559ce5f25e","timestamp":"2026-11-19T21:11:05.151Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffo