{"parentUuid":"585dfe85-b663-4fa9-b30e-165e559ec168","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011ChD2iLHEkSSSaj9HffDBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018jp8aPVcz3HQWy4bm2XjT8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-goeol\ngit add .gitattributes internal/setupui/shell_script_eol_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(windows): pin shell scripts to LF so a Windows clone can run them\n\nA CRLF checkout leaves a CR at the end of every line, and `sh` reads it as part\nof the last word on the line, so the script dies before doing any work. On\ncopies of this repository's own scripts:\n\n    mise-tasks/lint/gofmt      line 3: : command not found       exit 2\n    scripts/install-local.sh   line 2: set: -: invalid option    exit 2\n\ncore.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default, so that is what a stock\nWindows clone gets for all 22 of them. Nothing a pull request is checked on can\nsee it: the CI runners check out LF.\n\nThe companion commit pinned *.go for the same reason. Pinning by extension is\nnot enough here -- six of the scripts are the mise tasks, which carry shebangs\nand no extension, so `mise run lint:gofmt` would have stayed broken. The guard\ntherefore asks the filesystem which files begin with \"#!\" rather than trusting\ntheir names, and lives beside the repository's two other end-of-line guards.\n\nCheckout-only, as before: `git add --renormalize .` rewrites no file but\n.gitattributes itself, so no committed content changes. Commenting the two\nrules out turns the guard red naming all 22 scripts.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3\necho\necho \"=== branch state ===\"\ngit status --short --branch | head -3\ngit ls-remote --heads origin 'win/go-eol-lf' | wc -l | sed 's/^/remote branches named win\\/go-eol-lf: /'","description":"Commit the shell-script pin"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_read_input_tokens":185882,"output_tokens":836,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":836,"cache_read_input_tokens":185882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7379,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018jp8aPVcz3HQWy4bm2XjT8":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-goeol\ngit add .gitattributes internal/setupui/shell_script_eol_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(windows): pin shell scripts to LF so a Windows clone can run them\n\nA CRLF checkout leaves a CR at the end of every line, and `sh` reads it as part\nof the last word on the line, so the script dies before doing any work. On\ncopies of this repository's own scripts:\n\n    mise-tasks/lint/gofmt      line 3: : command not found       exit 2\n    scripts/install-local.sh   line 2: set: -: invalid option    exit 2\n\ncore.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default, so that is what a stock\nWindows clone gets for all 22 of them. Nothing a pull request is checked on can\nsee it: the CI runners check out LF.\n\nThe companion commit pinned *.go for the same reason. Pinning by extension is\nnot enough here -- six of the scripts are the mise tasks, which carry shebangs\nand no extension, so `mise run lint:gofmt` would have stayed broken. The guard\ntherefore asks the filesystem which files begin with \"#!\" rather than trusting\ntheir names, and lives beside the repository's two other end-of-line guards.\n\nCheckout-only, as before: `git add --renormalize .` rewrites no file but\n.gitattributes itself, so no committed content changes. Commenting the two\nrules out turns the guard red naming all 22 scripts.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3\necho\necho \"=== branch state ===\"\ngit status --short --branch | head -3\ngit ls-remote --heads origin 'win/go-eol-lf' | wc -l | sed 's/^/remote branches named win\\/go-eol-lf: /'","description":"Commit the shell-script pin"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"91ebfe5d-61fe-45dd-9b0b-4e125e707bbc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChD2iKzdUTJbChEZoCMzj","requestRef":"ffdf9323-60f0-4bfa-bc26-3ce0e7826067","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"96981a5e-4557-439c-9c78-07455b8e1e42","timestamp":"2026-11-19T21:54:06.317Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-goeol","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
